real arithmetic and ALTOPS.\n- `pytest -v cores/bench/test/`: PASS, all 11 pytest cases, including\n  expanded ALU and unchanged pipeline/retirement-gap suites in both real\n  and ALTOPS configurations (108.10 seconds).\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: PASS, selftest full-RVFI comparison\n  with ready buses and combined instruction/data stalls, plus canonical\n  stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/address validation.\n- Separately built the three unchanged random programs and ran all six\n  full-RVFI comparisons (each with ready buses and combined stalls): PASS.\n- `run_coremark_ipc`: PASS, including canonical CRCs, validation literal,\n  in-bounds accesses, completion, and both timing markers. Exactly\n  4,202,272 bracketed cycles for 10 iterations, unchanged from champion.\n- `python3 -m tools.eval.gowin bench --all-options`: PASS. Placement\n  options 0/1/2 measured 45.179 / 47.542 / 47.542 MHz; median 47.542 MHz.\n  Each used 3,968 logic cells, 890 registers, 8 LUT-RAMs, 6 BSRAMs, 6 DSPs.\n- Measured fitness: 47.542e6 * 10 / 4,202,272 = 113.134037968 iterations/s,\n  17.5052% above 96.28 and strictly above the 100.70888 acceptance threshold.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  PASS, all 53 checks, first attempt. Unchanged nret=1 wrapper/configuration\n  auto-selected; liveness and register consistency (`reg_ch0`) both passed.\n  No counterexamples, failures, or fix attempts.\n\nThe added subtractors and registered 3D increase area and fanout: +271\nlogic cells and +33 registers versus the stated champion. This implementation\ndoes not reproduce the prototype's 49.411 MHz median, but clears acceptance.\nThe option-0 worst path is now register-file-to-memory (27.429 ns, 14 cells).\nOptions 1/2 have a 26.329 ns register-file-to-memory worst path, closely\nfollowed by a 26.289 ns, 83-cell quotient-to-remainder divider path. No\nadditional optimization outside the proposed arithmetic change was made.\nFormal uses ALTOPS and does n