{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"agent_message","text":"The two failures come from the unchanged signed DIV/REM specifications being lowered to unsigned arithmetic (`bvudiv`/`bvurem`). For example, DIV of `0xf1aea008` by `0xffffffff` returns the RV32M-correct `0x0e515ff8`, while the deep checker expects zero. I’ll preserve the RTL and checker, add these counterexample operands to exact-result tests, and document formal-deep as non-passing.\n"}}
