d radix-8 restoring divmod network.\\nThe distinguishing optimization is eleven dependent digit stages with\\nparallel subtractors and a priority-free one-hot result mux, instead of\\nsixteen radix-4 stages or a serial bit-at-a-time divider. Preserve the\\ncombinational ALU interface and instruction latency, the champion's\\nexisting branch predictor, pipeline controls, and nret=1 contract.\\n\\nFor signed DIV/REM, convert both operan\n…[19125 of 22197 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:21a7891f3b70a2c8]…\n], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 74.76, \"delta_pct\": 458.74, \"vs_baseline\": 516.83, \"fmax_mhz\": 31.417, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4202272, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3819, \"ff\": 885, \"seeds\": [31.353, 31.417, 31.417], \"perturbations\": [[0, 31.353, 47], [1, 31.417, 48], [2, 31.417, 48]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_31_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_18_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -26.894, \"arrival_ns\": 37.189, \"logic_cells\": 250, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 47, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T17:31:07.057283Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r2s1 (improvement, +458.74%): Reusing eight restoring DIV/REM steps over four clocks shortens the combinational ALU path enough to outweigh added divide stalls, while launch/consume and a preceding load-use bubble still fit the 10-cycle retirement limit.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
