ly three dependent digit selections are needed per clock, and the\\nprevious external bottleneck has been removed. Increasing divide\\nlatency risks the established ten-cycle liveness limit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real divider's intra-cycle recurrence in rtl/alu.sv\\nwith three radix-4 restoring digit steps, leaving its request/busy/done/\\nconsume protocol and exact \n…[16611 of 19683 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5f96b30e19937c92]…\nline\": 848.84, \"fmax_mhz\": 48.327, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4202272, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3612, \"ff\": 857, \"seeds\": [46.994, 48.327, 48.327], \"perturbations\": [[0, 46.994, 31], [1, 48.327, 31], [2, 48.327, 31]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_1_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -16.279, \"arrival_ns\": 26.574, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 31, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T19:29:01.986021Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r5s1 (improvement, +19.44%): Predecoding the first two restoring DIV/REM steps at launch with a small-divisor case network shortens feedback from six subtract/select stages to five and removes the final-step mux, improving median Fmax from 40.459 to 48.327 MHz while preserving six iteration clocks and CoreMark's 4,202,272 cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
