ercent above 128.30, using the median of the existing Gowin\n  placement options. The expected gain is an estimate pending prototype\n  validation; no contract, evaluator, benchmark or other core may change.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 12\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the indexed register array with 31 independently enabled\n      scalar word registers, explicit per-port one-hot address decoding,\n      masked word leaves and balanced static OR read trees. Keep x0\n      constant, synchronous reset, synchronous writes and the exact\n      combinational write-first bypass priority. Verify fabric-flop mapping.\n  - file: test/test_reg_file.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing tests and add a deterministic scoreboard covering\n      every read-address pair, repeated writes, both-port bypass collisions,\n      x0 priority, disabled writes and reset/write collision. Compare\n      architectural port values before and after edges without depending\n      on the implementation's internal register names.\nYAML\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r7s0.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated hypothesis is schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated hypothesis is schema valid\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
