{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_73", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport yaml\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r7s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r7s0','title':'Flatten forwarding and ALU operand selection into one-hot muxes','category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 128.30 at 53.914 MHz with 4,202,272 CoreMark cycles.\nIts worst reported path starts in the register file and crosses execute\ncontrol. Prior micro_opt attempts targeted divider arithmetic, squash\nfanout and M-extension selection. Temporary probes on this champion found\nthat squash-only separation reached 53.600 MHz and a flop register file\nreached 54.934 MHz, both below acceptance. Their remaining paths traverse\noperand forwarding and arithmetic. The current EX code encodes forwarding\npriority, decodes it in a wide case mux, then adds a second PC/immediate\nmux before the ALU. Flattening this serial selection is a local timing\nopportunity without adding cycles or changing prediction or arithmetic.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Make one local operand-delivery optimization: express the forwarding and\nALU operand muxes as parallel one-hot masked-OR selections, preserving\nall existing register boundaries and operand-source priorities.\n\nIn forward_unit compute EX/MEM and retained normal-MEM/WB hits in parallel\nfor each source, including reg_write and nonzero destination guards.\nDrive select bit 0 from the EX hit and bit 1 from WB_hit && \"'!EX_hit.\nBoth bits remain mutually exclusive, with 00 selecting the ID/EX value;\nthe existing two-bit interface and its 00/01/10 encodings remain intact.\nDo not gate retained-WB ownership with its retirement-valid pulse.\n\nIn ex_stage form local_select = !(|fwd_select). Produce architectural\nrs1/rs2 with an OR of three masked words: the ID/EX operand, EX/MEM ALU\nresult and ordinary MEM/WB data. Use these values for branches, JALR,\neffective addresses, stores, divide operand snapshots and RVFI exactly\nas before. For ALU inputs, flatten the additional selection into the\nsame network: alu_a selects PC when is_auipc, otherwise one of the three\nrs1 sources; alu_b selects immediate when alu_src, otherwise one of the\nthree rs2 sources. Include !is_auipc or !alu_src in each corresponding\nregister-source mask. Compute masks independently of operand data and\nuse balanced OR expressions, avoiding a second wide mux after forwarding.\n\nAll priority and x0 rules remain unchanged. Every live consumer must\nreceive the youngest matching value, including two writers to the same\nregister and held ordinary WB during memory stalls. Keep direct divider\ncompletion restricted to the existing register-file write/write-first\npath; it must not enter the ordinary EX forwarding network. Keep the\nregister file, ALU arithmetic, divider schedule, ID/EX squash, branch\npredictor, memory handshakes and single-channel RVFI contract unchanged.\n\nThe expected benefit is fewer dependent LUT mux levels before the\nmultiplier, branch comparator and effective-address adder. Extra mask\nfanout or synthesis refactoring may reduce the benefit; evaluate the\nmapped vendor timing rather than assuming an RTL depth reduction.\nValidate mask exclusivity and equivalence for local/EX/WB sources,\nx0, simultaneous matches, write enables, PC/immediate overrides,\nretained WB under bus holds and direct divide completion consumers.\nRun existing real/ALTOPS pipeline tests, unchanged formal checks and\nready/stalled full-RVFI cosimulation. Preserve all liveness, arithmetic,\ndecoder, CRC, UART, address-bound and timing-marker checks.\n\nCanonical CoreMark cycles should remain exactly 4,202,272 for the same\nstall sequence. Acceptance requires measured fitness strictly above\n134.2018, more than 4.6 percent above 128.30, using the median of the\nexisting Gowin placement options. No evaluator, contract, benchmark,\nother core or nret declaration may change.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':9,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[{'file':'rtl/forward_unit.sv','description':'Compute parallel EX and WB hits and expose mutually exclusive select bits directly, preserving EX-over-WB priority, x0 suppression and retained-WB ownership without retirement-valid gating.'},{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace encoded wide forwarding cases with one-hot masked-OR networks. Fold AUIPC PC and immediate selection into parallel ALU source masks, while retaining separate correctly forwarded rs1/rs2 for all architectural uses and divide snapshots.'},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all tests and add directed EX source-selection equivalence checks across local/EX/WB sources, simultaneous writers, PC/immediate overrides and x0. Preserve held-WB forwarding, divide completion, operand RVFI, bus-stall, squash and retirement-gap assertions.'}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False))\nimport json,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('One-hot forwarding hypothesis written and schema validated')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
