{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_79", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r7s0.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='One-hot operand delivery from flop register file through EX'\nh['motivation']='''The champion scores 128.30 at 53.914 MHz and 4,202,272 CoreMark cycles.\nIts worst reported path starts in the register file and crosses execute\ncontrol. Earlier micro_opt attempts targeted divider arithmetic, recovery\nfanout and M-extension selection. Local probes on this champion identify\ntwo limits in operand delivery: a BSRAM register-file launch feeding long\nexecute paths, and the serial forwarding/ALU operand mux chain. Squash-only\nseparation reached 53.600 MHz, explicit flop storage alone 54.934 MHz, and\none-hot EX forwarding alone 53.256 MHz. None clears acceptance alone;\nthis proposal applies one-hot selection throughout the operand path.'''\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'].replace('Make one local operand-delivery optimization: express the forwarding and\\\\nALU operand muxes as parallel one-hot masked-OR selections, preserving\\\\nall existing register boundaries and operand-source priorities.','''Make one local operand-delivery optimization: use explicit flop storage\nand parallel one-hot read/forward/ALU source selection throughout the\nregister-file-to-EX path. Preserve the external register-file interface,\nexisting pipeline boundaries, operand priorities and every instruction's\nlatency. This is a micro-optimization of storage mapping and mux topology.\n\nIn reg_file implement x1 through x31 as independent 32-bit word registers\ninside constant-index generate blocks. Each has synchronous reset and\nlocal write enable w_en && w_addr == its constant index; do not store x0.\nFor each read port decode the address into mutually exclusive per-word\nselects, mask the words and combine them with a balanced binary OR tree.\nInclude a constant-zero x0 leaf. Use statically indexed wiring, avoiding\nvariable-index RAM reads and serial procedural OR accumulators. Verify\nGowin maps this to fabric flops and retains fabric operand capture at\nID/EX, rather than folding those operand registers into BSRAM read ports.\nPreserve final read priority: x0 returns zero, otherwise a same-address\nenabled write returns w_data, otherwise return the stored word. Reset\nstill clears every stored word even when a write is simultaneously enabled.\nAll 32 bits and both independent read ports remain architecturally exact.''').replace('register file, ALU arithmetic, divider schedule, ID/EX squash, branch','ALU arithmetic, divider schedule, ID/EX squash, branch').replace('multiplier, branch comparator and effective-address adder. Extra mask\\\\nfanout or synthesis refactoring may reduce the benefit; evaluate the','multiplier, branch comparator and effective-address adder, together with\\\\nremoval of the slow BSRAM launch. Extra flops, mask fanout, read-mux area\\\\nand routing or synthesis refactoring may reduce the benefit; evaluate the')\nh['hypothesis'] += '''\\\\n\\\\nRetain every register-file test and add a deterministic scoreboard for\nall 1024 read-address pairs after distinct writes, repeated overwrites,\nx0 writes, bypass collisions on either/both read ports, disabled writes\nand reset/write collisions. Include the direct divide completion-to-ID\nwrite-first path and retained ordinary WB during memory holds in pipeline\nvalidation. Do not change reset behavior or relax any correctness gate.\n'''\nh['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']=10\nh['changes'].insert(0,{'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'Use 31 independent scalar word registers with synchronous reset and local write enables; per-port one-hot read decoding, masked leaves and balanced OR trees. Preserve x0 and write-first bypass priority exactly. Verify fabric-flop storage and ID/EX operand capture in the vendor netlist.'})\nh['changes'].append({'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'Retain existing tests and add a deterministic port-level scoreboard covering all read-address pairs, repeated writes, both-port bypass, x0, disabled writes and reset/write collisions.'})\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,default_style=None))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Combined operand-path hypothesis is schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
