CH/JAL target-selection bit lets EX recover via direction XOR (except offset +4) instead of a selected 32-bit next-PC comparison, shortening the redirect path without changing CoreMark cycles while JALR keeps a separate full-width comparison.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-001-r5s0 (regression, +17.50%): Registering 34-bit 3D at launch lets three radix-4 steps with par\n…[117912 of 120984 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c7e5a54fb2121707]…\nt\": 11.97, \"vs_baseline\": 1295.3, \"fmax_mhz\": 71.063, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4202272, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5021, \"ff\": 1858, \"seeds\": [65.005, 71.063, 71.063], \"perturbations\": [[0, 65.005, 11], [1, 71.063, 11], [2, 71.063, 11]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_23_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_31_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -10.383, \"arrival_ns\": 20.678, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_wb\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T21:43:57.782632Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r8s1 (improvement, +11.97%): Overlapping registered 3D preparation with four narrow fabric prefix steps enables two radix-4 stages per later clock without extra divide latency, while avoiding a prefix ROM prevents Gowin BSRAM output delay from negating the shorter recurrence.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
