{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith(('r4s1','r4s0')):\n  print(d['id'])\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\ncat cores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-001-r4s0\nMake one local control-cone optimization: remove flush and redirect\nfrom the combinational instruction payload and from ID/EX payload\nwrite enables. Carry raw imem_data through IF/ID even on a killed or\nunavailable fetch, and implement bubbles at the ID/EX validity and\ncontrol boundary. Keep every pipeline stage, branch prediction policy,\ninstruction latency, divider schedule and external handshake intact.\n\nIn if_stage, drive out.instr directly from imem_data, retaining the\nexisting out.valid qualification and prediction metadata. Preserve\nreset and redirect priority in the PC update, including recovery\nwhile imemReady is low. Raw payload bits on an invalid bundle are\nirrelevant; the instruction must never acquire live controls.\n\nIn id_stage, separate payload capture from squash control. Reset\nretains its defined initialization. Otherwise capture pc, prediction,\noperands, immediate, register addresses and instruction whenever\n!stall, without qualifying this payload enable or zeroing these\nfields with flush, redirect or in.valid. For ctrl and valid only,\npreserve priority: reset clears; flush clears even if stall is also\nasserted; otherwise stall holds; otherwise a valid fetch captures\ndecoded controls and valid=1, and an invalid fetch captures ctrl='0\nand valid=0. A stalled instruction's full payload and controls remain\nstable. Clearing controls as well as valid is essential because the\nexisting memory, hazard and forwarding logic examines controls without\nuniversally gating them by validity. Do not change legal decoding or\nrely on valid alone to suppress writes, memory requests or forwarding.\n\nIn hazard_unit, compare the now-raw source fields for load-use, with\nimem_ready qualifying that dependency. Do not gate the source fields\nor dependency comparison with redirect, flush_if or out.valid: those\nwould reintroduce recovery into the operand-selection path. Recovery\nalready overrides PC hold, and flush_id already overrides ID/EX hold\nwhen EX advances. Preserve dmem and execute-wait hold prior\n…[5715 of 8787 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0f6cb9a06f476b2b]…\nUART,\naddress-bound and marker checks, retiring ten benchmark iterations\nin exactly 4,202,272 bracketed cycles. Combining that cycle count\nwith median vendor Fmax gives fitness 96.3336, 17.95 percent above\nthe 81.67 champion. The prototype RTL is restored after measurement;\nthis file specifies the implementation to reproduce and revalidate.\n\nPreserve the narrow prototype scope: raw fetch payload, independent\nID/EX validity, valid-only divide bubbles, valid-qualified hazards\nand side effects, and one extra retained WB forwarding-valid bit.\nDo not expand the change into a stage addition or a divider redesign;\nthe newly limiting divider sets a practical ceiling on this proposal.\nThese measurements do not replace the final implementation's formal,\ncosim and median Gowin evaluation. Acceptance requires measured\nfitness strictly above 85.42682, 4.6 percent above the 81.67 champion.\nPreserve all decoder legality checks, real and ALTOPS arithmetic,\nten-cycle liveness coverage, nret=1 ports and every hard invariant.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
