{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r7s1.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-002-r7s1',\n 'title':'Flop-banked register file with a physical operand-register boundary',\n 'category':'structural',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 128.30 at 53.914 MHz and 4,202,272 CoreMark cycles.\nA fresh Gowin option-0 run reproduces 50.289 MHz: its 25.179 ns worst path\nstarts at the register-file BSRAM output, passes through operand selection\nand JALR recovery, and ends at ID/EX reset. The inferred memory has absorbed\npart of the operand capture boundary: BSRAM clock-to-output and read bypass\nlogic remain ahead of EX forwarding. Previous structural hypotheses mostly\nretimed division; r4s1 changed validity, and r6s1 separated arithmetic completion\nfrom memory addressing. The remaining register-file storage topology is a\nnew structural opportunity. Retain single-cycle issue and move the raw\nregister read mux ahead of explicit operand flops by changing the RF storage.\n''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Make one structural change: replace the inferred two-read register-file\nmemory with 31 explicit, independently written 32-bit flop banks, and read\nthem through decoded one-hot selection and balanced OR trees. The existing\nID/EX operand registers must remain a real physical pipeline boundary,\nseparating register selection from EX forwarding, arithmetic and recovery.\nKeep the architectural register_file interface and all pipeline cycle\nboundaries unchanged; this is a storage and operand-collection topology\nchange, not an added pipeline stage or an ISA change.\n\nGive each x1..x31 bank a statically elaborated data register and a local\nwrite enable w_en && w_addr == bank_number. Reset each bank to zero as\nbefore. Do not code the bank writes as a variable-index memory access, and\ndo not code reads as regs[rs_addr]; these encourage the same inferred BSRAM\nand output-register absorption as the champion. Decode each read address\nonce into 31 one-hot selects, mask each bank's word, and OR the selected\nwords with an explicitly balanced tree if needed to keep synthesis from\nbuilding a serial priority chain. x0 is a constant zero and has no writable\nbank. Preserve the exact same-cycle write-first read bypass, including\npriority of x0 over bypass and independent matching for rs1 and rs2.\n\nUse portable synthesizable SystemVerilog and structurally elaborated fixed\nbank accesses. No vendor black boxes or simulation-only implementation may\nreplace the functional register file. Verify in Gowin's synthesis report\nthat the RF is implemented as flop banks and that ID/EX operand values have\nphysical flop endpoints rather than only registered RAM addresses and\npost-RAM bypass logic. The expected cost is about 992 storage flops plus\nread selection logic, offset by removing the two RF BSRAMs. Keep within the\nTang Nano 20K's resources and the 10,000-LUT target. All 32 architectural\nbits and all source/destination addresses remain fully supported.\n\nPreserve the current EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB forwarding priority, retained WB\nownership during memory stalls, ordinary write-first decode behavior, and\ndirect divide completion writes into the RF. Leave branch prediction,\nrecovery timing, divider/multiplier arithmetic and latency, dedicated\nmemory address path, memory handshakes, decoder legality and nret=1 unchanged.\nThus the canonical stalled CoreMark interval should remain 4,202,272 cycles;\nany difference must be explained as a bug or unintended scope change before\nacceptance. The intended fitness gain comes from higher Fmax only.\n\nRun existing register-file, real/ALTOPS pipeline and arithmetic tests,\nunchanged formal gates, and full-RVFI selftest/random cosimulation with and\nwithout stalls. Retain all reset/x0/write-first checks and cover writes and\nreads of every register, simultaneous same-address reads, distinct read\nports, back-to-back writes, all data bits, and divide-completion-to-decode\nbypass under fetch stalls. Preserve canonical CoreMark CRCs, UART text,\naddress bounds, marker timing and the ten-cycle liveness bound.\n\nCompare median Gowin Fmax times measured iterations/cycle, not cell counts\nalone. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 134.2018, or approximately\n56.395 MHz if the cycle count is unchanged. The primary risks are routing\ncongestion from the extra flops/read trees and a newly limiting divider or\nmultiplier path. Do not add unrelated arithmetic or predictor changes if\nthose paths become limiting; report the measured result for this one\nstructural hypothesis. Any prototype evidence appended below is preliminary\nand must be reproduced by the implementation phase.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':12,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'''Replace the indexed inferred RF memory with 31 explicit resettable flop\nbanks, local decoded synchronous write enables, shared read-address\none-hot decoders and balanced masked-OR read trees. Preserve x0 and both\nwrite-first bypass ports exactly. Ensure synthesis retains the existing\nID/EX operand flops rather than absorbing them into inferred BSRAM reads.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'''Retain all existing reset, x0 and same-cycle write-first tests. Add\ncomplete bank and data-bit coverage, two-port same/different-address reads,\nback-to-back writes and reset after populated state against an independent\n32-register reference model. No timing or architectural check is relaxed.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain the original stage timing, branch-token, forwarding, direct divide\ncompletion, startup and ten-cycle liveness assertions. Extend operand\ncollection tests across bank boundaries and same-cycle normal/divide WB\nwith stalls, checking exact RVFI operands and results and held forwarding.\n'''}]\n}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef str_rep(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,str_rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\nprint('Wrote and validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
