ites and\nreads of every register, simultaneous same-address reads, distinct read\nports, back-to-back writes, all data bits, and divide-completion-to-decode\nbypass under fetch stalls. Preserve canonical CoreMark CRCs, UART text,\naddress bounds, marker timing and the ten-cycle liveness bound.\n\nCompare median Gowin Fmax times measured iterations/cycle, not cell counts\nalone. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 134.2018, or approximately\n56.395 MHz if the cycle count is unchanged. The primary risks are routing\ncongestion from the extra flops/read trees and a newly limiting divider or\nmultiplier path. Do not add unrelated arithmetic or predictor changes if\nthose paths become limiting; report the measured result for this one\nstructural hypothesis. Any prototype evidence appended below is preliminary\nand must be reproduced by the implementation phase.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':12,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'''Replace the indexed inferred RF memory with 31 explicit resettable flop\nbanks, local decoded synchronous write enables, shared read-address\none-hot decoders and balanced masked-OR read trees. Preserve x0 and both\nwrite-first bypass ports exactly. Ensure synthesis retains the existing\nID/EX operand flops rather than absorbing them into inferred BSRAM reads.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'''Retain all existing reset, x0 and same-cycle write-first tests. Add\ncomplete bank and data-bit coverage, two-port same/different-address reads,\nback-to-back writes and reset after populated state against an independent\n32-register reference model. No timing or architectural check is relaxed.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain the original stage timing, branch-token, forwarding, direct divide\ncompletion, startup and ten-cycle liveness assertions. Extend operand\ncollection tests across bank boundaries and same-cycle normal/divide WB\nwith stalls, checking exact RVFI operands and results and held forwarding.\n'''}]\n}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef str_rep(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,str_rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\nprint('Wrote and validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Wrote and validated cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r7s1.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
