{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r7s1.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Register operand delivery before EX forwarding and recovery'\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('Make one structural change: replace the inferred two-read register-file\\\\nmemory with 31 explicit, independently written 32-bit flop banks, and read\\\\nthem through decoded one-hot selection and balanced OR trees.', 'Make one structural change: move register selection and source/destination\\\\nmatching ahead of a physical operand-delivery boundary. Use 31 explicit,\\\\nindependently written 32-bit RF flop banks with decoded one-hot reads, and\\\\nregister forwarding-match tokens alongside the existing ID/EX operands.')\ns='''\nPrecompute four equality tokens in decode: incoming rs1/rs2 versus the\ncurrent ID/EX destination (which will become EX/MEM), and versus the current\nEX/MEM destination (which will become MEM/WB). Register these tokens on the\nsame edge that accepts the associated instruction into ID/EX. Reset and\nflush clear them; a true ID/EX hold retains them. EX forwarding consumes\nthese registered equalities instead of doing five-bit comparisons in its\ncritical cycle. Continue qualifying each match with the actual live source's\nreg_write and nonzero destination, and keep EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB-over-register\npriority. Registering equality alone avoids predicting eventual write\neligibility: alignment traps, bubbles and the divider's direct retirement\ncan still cancel an apparent producer before it reaches a forwarding slot.\n\nKeep the retained ordinary WB source and match tokens stable across an\nolder dmem hold even after its retirement pulse clears. During divider\nwaiting the older slots drain, but division uses operands captured at\nlaunch; no stale match token may resample operands or determine completion.\nA younger instruction accepted on direct divide retirement uses the\nexisting RF write-first path, and its new tokens must reflect the now-empty\nordinary EX/MEM/WB slots. Do not forward the direct result through the\nordinary WB-to-EX input. Test load-use bubbles, recovery plus holds,\nback-to-back writes to one destination, trap-cancelled writers and all\ndivide consumers. No additional operand stage or dependency bubble is added.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('Preserve the current EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB forwarding priority,',s+'\\\\nPreserve the current EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB forwarding priority,')\nd['changes'].insert(1,{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Register the four decode-time source/destination equality tokens with exactly the ID/EX accept, hold, flush and reset schedule. Compare incoming source addresses to the producers that will occupy EX/MEM and MEM/WB on the next cycle; wire tokens to the forwarding unit. Preserve external IO and every pipeline latency.'})\nd['changes'].insert(2,{'file':'rtl/forward_unit.sv','description':'Consume registered match tokens instead of live five-bit source/destination comparisons. Keep live reg_write/nonzero-rd eligibility, EX/MEM-first priority, ordinary retained-WB ownership and x0 semantics.'})\nd['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']=10\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda dumper,data:dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\nprint('Updated hypothesis, schema valid')\nPY\npytest -q cores/bench/test > /srv/hwebench/tmp/92f133a1/4e0ba974/r7s1-operands-tests.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
