{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261002-001-r7s0|hyp-20261002-001-r5s0|hyp-20261002-002-r6s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Replace combinational division with a bounded iterative execute unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median\\nFmax 5.442 MHz, 12312 LUT4s, and a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path\\nthrough forwarding and u_ex/u_alu. No LESSONS.md or previous structural\\nattempts are present. The ALU currently synthesizes signed and unsigned\\ndivision and remainder as combinational / and % operators. These are a\\nstrong candidate for the unusually deep execute path, although the\\nrecorded module-level timing report does not identify individual operators.\\nEvery instruction pays the resulting clock-period cost. Sharing a bounded\\nsequential divide/remainder datapath should substantially improve Fmax\\nand reduce logic area at the cost of extra cycles on DIV/REM instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median\\nFmax 5.442 MHz, 12312 LUT4s, and a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path\\nthrough forwarding and u_ex/u_alu. No LESSONS.md or previous structural\\nattempts are present. The ALU currently synthesizes signed and unsigned\\ndivision and remainder as combinational / and % operators. These are a\\nstrong candidate for the unusually deep execute path, although the\\nrecorded module-level timing report does not identify individual operators.\\nEvery instruction pays the resulting clock-period cost. Sharing a bounded\\nsequential divide/remainder datapath should substantially improve Fmax\\nand reduce logic area at the cost of extra cycles on DIV/REM instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make precisely one structural change: decouple DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU\\nfrom the single-cycle ALU into a shared multicycle execute resource.\\nKeep the existing pipeline, single retirement channel, multiplication,\\nbranch policy, register file and memory interfaces. Implement the resource\\ninside alu.sv and extend its internal interface with clock/reset and a\\nstart/completion/consume handshak\n…[119332 of 122404 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a63f5c8f74bb323a]…\nUTs, and **no BSRAM/SSRAM**. The four BSRAMs belong to core_bench's\\n  benchmark memories. u_id retains 156 registers; the core has four local\\n  token registers.\\n- Option-0 `impl/pnr/core_bench.tr` explicitly terminates a setup path at\\n  `cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_24_s0/D`, with a physical CLK pin/setup check.\\n- Option-1/2 timing reports likewise terminate paths at\\n  `cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_29_s0/D` and bits 5, 9, 7, and 2, each with\\n  physical CLK/setup checks. Both operand values remain physical flops.\\n\\nThe limiting option-0 path is now inside the unchanged divider:\\n`divisor_q_3_s0` to `remainder_q_3_s1`, arrival 22.725 ns, 127 reported\\ncells. Options 1/2 are limited by `quotient_q_31_s1` to `remainder_q_0_s1`,\\n21.763 ns, 119 cells. Arithmetic was deliberately left unchanged as required.\\nRemaining concern is placement/routing sensitivity and divider timing;\\nthere are no known functional failures or architectural deviations.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T20:58:31.044630Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 7}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
