{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(s)\n if r['id'] in ('hyp-20261002-001-r2s0','hyp-20261002-001-r3s0','hyp-20261002-001-r5s0'):\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('\\\\n',r['id'],r.get('title'))\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261002-001-r2s0 Shared radix-8 combinational divider with one-hot digit selection\nReplace only real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic in rtl/alu.sv with one\nshared, explicitly unrolled unsigned radix-8 restoring divmod network.\nThe distinguishing optimization is eleven dependent digit stages with\nparallel subtractors and a priority-free one-hot result mux, instead of\nsixteen radix-4 stages or a serial bit-at-a-time divider. Preserve the\ncombinational ALU interface and instruction latency, the champion's\nexisting branch predictor, pipeline controls, and nret=1 contract.\n\nFor signed DIV/REM, convert both operands to unsigned two's-complement\nmagnitudes; for DIVU/REMU use the raw operands. Precompute the unsigned\nmultiples M[k] = k*D for k=1..7 in 35 bits, with explicit zero extension\nbefore shifts or additions. Use wiring for D, 2D, and 4D, and parallel\nshift/add or shift/sub expressions for 3D, 5D, 6D, and 7D; do not build\na serial chain of seven additions or infer multipliers for constants.\n\nConsume dividend bits [31:30] in an initial two-bit stage, followed by\nten three-bit stages consuming [29:27] down to [2:0]. Start with R=0.\nAt each stage concatenate the previous remainder and the next dividend\ngroup to form T. The total prefix width W is 2, 5, 8, ..., 32; T fits\nwithin W bits because the previous remainder never exceeds the consumed\ndividend prefix. Keep these widths static and explicit in generate\nblocks so early stages use narrow arithmetic.\n\nFor each k=1..7, calculate diff[k] = {0,T} - {0,M[k][W-1:0]} in W+1\nunsigned bits, all in parallel. Set ge[k] only when diff[k][W] is zero\nAND M[k][34:W] is zero. The upper-bit guard must be retained even at\nW=32: a truncated large divisor multiple must never be accepted.\nIn the first stage only k=1..3 are needed and the quotient digit is\ntwo bits; all later stages use k=1..7 and three-bit digits.\n\nLet K be 3 for the first stage and 7 otherwise. Define ge[0]=1 and\nge[K+1]=0. Since the exact comparisons are monotone, the winning digit\nhas onehot[k] = ge[k] AND NOT \n…[9571 of 12643 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1590d1a58a493087]…\nhanged single-retirement formal configuration\npassed, including liveness and register consistency. That formal run\nuses ALTOPS; real arithmetic was exercised by the expanded ALU vectors\nand cosimulation, not claimed proven by the ALTOPS checks. The temporary\nprototype RTL and test edits were restored after measurement.\nThese measurements are prototype evidence; the final implementation\nmust rerun correctness gates and median vendor timing.\n\nThe parallel subtractors and four-way selection increase area/fanout,\nand magnitude-to-3D generation can become a new launch path. Keep the\nproposal limited to this arithmetic change. Validate real and ALTOPS\nALU tests, existing pipeline and retirement-gap tests, unchanged formal\nand stalled full-RVFI cosim, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/address/\nmarker checks. Preserve every invariant and the nret=1 contract.\nAcceptance requires measured fitness strictly above 100.70888, more\nthan 4.6 percent above 96.28; at unchanged cycles this needs median\nFmax above 42.320611 MHz.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
