{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_61", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r8s1.yaml')\ns=p.read_text()\na=s.index('hypothesis: |')\nb=s.index('expected_impact:',a)\nh='''hypothesis: |\n  Make one structural change to the sequential divider: overlap preparation\n  of a registered 3D operand with a compact first-four-bit operation, then\n  reuse a two-step radix-4 digit resource for the remaining seven clocks.\n  Keep launch, eight busy clocks, completion retention and direct retirement\n  exactly as in the champion. The new preparation/iteration decomposition\n  must add no clock, pipeline stage or retirement channel. In particular,\n  do not put 3D generation after magnitude conversion on the launch path.\n\n  Launch captures the same signed/unsigned magnitudes, original dividend,\n  signs and exceptions as today, initializes R=0, and places the dividend\n  magnitude in Q. On busy iteration zero, register 3D in 34 bits from the\n  already registered divisor, using zero extension BEFORE shift/add:\n  dwide={2'b0,divisor_q}; triple_q=(dwide<<1)+dwide. D remains available\n  in divisor_q and 2D is wiring. Hold triple_q through all later iterations.\n\n  Simultaneously consume the first four dividend bits with a small exact\n  table. T=Q[31:28] is only four bits. If D>=16 the quotient digit is zero\n  and the remainder is T. For D=1..15, a statically elaborated combinational\n  table over {D[3:0],T} produces {floor(T/D)[3:0],(T mod D)[3:0]}.\n  Guard this table with D[31:4]==0. For D=0 choose digit 15 and remainder T;\n  retain the existing final architectural divide-by-zero override. Generate\n  constants at elaboration or emit a complete 256-entry case statement;\n  never infer live division or modulo. Register Q={Q[27:0],digit} and the\n  zero-extended four-bit remainder on this same iteration-zero edge.\n  There is no added ROM latency; synthesis may absorb this existing capture\n  into block RAM. Thus useful first-digit work hides the 3D preparation.\n\n  On busy iterations one through seven use exactly TWO radix-4 restoring\n  steps in series, consuming four dividend bits total per clock. Each step\n  forms the 34-bit T={R,Q[31:30]}. Compute THREE parallel 35-bit unsigned\n  differences against exact 34-bit D,2D,3D. The leading difference bit is\n  borrow; let ge1,ge2,ge3 be its inverse for each multiple. Decode one-hot\n  winner bits w0=\"'!ge1, w1=ge1&&!ge2, w2=ge2&&!ge3, w3=ge3. Select the\n  next remainder by balanced OR of the four masked low-32-bit candidates\n  T,diff1,diff2,diff3; append digit {w2|w3,w1|w3} to Q[29:0]. The second\n  identical step consumes the first step'\"'s R and Q, and its outputs become\n  the registered iteration result. Avoid priority muxes and a second\n  subtraction after digit selection. Keep all 34-bit multiples and 35-bit\n  differences until borrow is known: truncation falsely accepts large D.\n  For nonzero D, R<D gives T<4D and the chosen remainder fits 32 bits.\n  Four initial bits plus seven four-bit iteration groups consume all 32 bits.\n\n  Keep current result sign correction, exceptional RV32M results, stable\n  done/result until consume, reset cancellation, launch operand capture and\n  exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas. ALTOPS keeps the same eight busy clocks\n  and excludes the real digit arithmetic. Preserve the direct completion\n  path, ordinary retained WB forwarding, effective-address path, decoder,\n  prediction, multiplier, memory handshakes, full RV32 width and nret=1.\n\n  This reduces the recurrent path from four dependent full-width binary\n  subtract/select stages to two radix-4 stages. A registered 3D bank avoids\n  recalculating multiples inside that recurrence; overlapping its preparation\n  avoids a new operand-launch bottleneck. The area tradeoff is six trial\n  subtractors in place of four, a 34-bit bank register and a small constant\n  first-digit table. Stay within device capacity and the 10,000-LUT target.\n  Do not add unrelated branch, memory, multiplier or pipeline changes.\n\n  Preliminary exploration measured a larger one-step radix-16 resource\n  using this same first-digit/preparation overlap. It passed arithmetic,\n  pipeline, all 53 standard formal checks, selftest/random RVFI cosimulation\n  with and without stalls, and canonical CoreMark at 4,202,272 measured\n  cycles. However, its 64.987 MHz median gave only about 2.4 percent gain,\n  below acceptance, with 5,781 logic cells, 2,114 registers and five BSRAMs.\n  Its worst paths had moved to ordinary WB/multiply and branch-update logic.\n  Therefore the proposed final resource uses TWO radix-4 steps and only 3D\n  storage to reduce routing pressure while still shortening the divider.\n  The large radix-16 measurement is negative evidence, not a claimed result\n  for this smaller final implementation.\n\n  Retain all existing arithmetic/protocol assertions. Extend real ALU tests\n  across all first-nibble/small-divisor combinations, every radix-4 digit,\n  divisors near powers of two and 0xffffffff, upper-multiple rejection,\n  signed extremes, zero divisors and seeded full-width random operands\n  against an independent integer reference. Check eight busy iterations,\n  changed live inputs after launch, held completion, consecutive operations\n  and reset at every phase. Exercise changing divisors so stale 3D state\n  cannot pass. Run real/ALTOPS pipeline tests, unchanged formal gates and\n  stalled full-RVFI cosimulation, including load-to-divide and consecutive\n  divides under the existing ten-cycle retirement bound. Standard formal\n  uses ALTOPS; it does not prove real division arithmetic. Use exact-result\n  testing and formal-deep when feasible without altering any checker.\n\n  Canonical CoreMark should retain exactly 4,202,272 bracketed cycles,\n  all five CRCs, required UART text and address bounds. A cycle change needs\n  explanation before acceptance. Prior dynamic measurement found zero\n  divides in the timed interval, but this must remain a general RV32IM\n  resource. Accept only measured fitness strictly above 157.97738 iter/s,\n  more than 4.6 percent above 151.03, requiring about 66.3864 MHz at the\n  existing cycle count. Evaluate median Gowin Fmax times measured\n  iterations/cycle, including any new limiting path and area cost.\n'''\ns=s[:a]+h+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('Overlap divisor-bank preparation with the first radix-16 digit','Overlap divisor preparation with the first quotient digit')\ns=s.replace('registered divisor-multiple bank and one parallel digit-selection\\\\n  resource','registered divisor operand and fewer parallel digit-selection\\\\n  stages')\ns=s.replace('fitness_delta_pct: 12','fitness_delta_pct: 8')\na=s.index('changes:')\ns=s[:a]+'''changes:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Overlap a compact first-four-bit divide table and registered 34-bit 3D\n      preparation on busy iteration zero; use two radix-4 parallel-trial\n      steps per later iteration. Preserve all ALU ports, launch/eight-clock/\n      consume timing, sign/exception handling, ALTOPS and other operations.\n      Keep 3D generation off the launch and recurrent arithmetic paths.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every existing assertion and vector. Add exact first-digit,\n      all-digit, wide-multiple, boundary and randomized arithmetic coverage,\n      alternating divisors and unchanged eight-clock completion, input\n      independence, result retention and reset checks in both configurations.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all architectural and stage-timing checks. Extend divide\n      sequences across 3D reinitialization, alternating small/large and\n      signed/unsigned divisors, producer/consumer hazards, memory holds and\n      fetch stalls; verify exact RVFI data, single retirement, cancellation\n      and the ten-cycle liveness bound.\n'''\np.write_text(s)\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(s),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined hypothesis written and schema valid.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
