{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r8s1.yaml');s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('Overlap divisor preparation with the first quotient digit','Fabric-first divider preparation with two radix-4 steps')\ns=s.replace('of a registered 3D operand with a compact first-four-bit operation, then','of a registered 3D operand with a narrow fabric first-four-bit operation, then')\na=s.index('  Simultaneously consume the first four dividend bits')\nb=s.index('  On busy iterations one through seven',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''  Simultaneously consume the first four dividend bits using FOUR NARROW\n  binary restoring steps in fabric. Initialize a four-bit prefix remainder\n  r=0 and four-bit prefix quotient q=Q[31:28]. Each step forms five-bit\n  t={r,q[3]} and six-bit diff={1'b0,t}-{2'b0,D[3:0]}. A successful\n  subtraction requires BOTH \"'!diff[5] and D[31:4]==0. Select the next r\n  from diff[3:0] on success or t[3:0] otherwise, and shift q left one bit\n  appending the success flag. After four steps, register Q={Q[27:0],q}\n  and R={28'\"'b0,r}. The consumed dividend prefix never exceeds 15, so all\n  prefix remainders fit four bits. For D>=16 every step rejects subtraction;\n  for D=0 every step accepts, yielding digit 15 and the unmodified prefix\n  remainder, compatible with the existing divide-by-zero result override.\n  The high-divisor guard is mandatory, including D with low nibble zero.\n\n  Implement this prefix network with explicit narrow wires/subtractions,\n  not an indexed ROM or complete case-table that Gowin can map into BSRAM.\n  Keep the prefix result and subsequent remainder in physical fabric flops.\n  A prototype table was absorbed into BSRAM and put its slow output on the\n  next full-width feedback path, negating the shorter digit recurrence.\n  Check the synthesis resource/path report for this structural boundary:\n  no divider BSRAM, and no BSRAM launch into the quotient/remainder loop.\n  Preparing 3D and the four-bit prefix in parallel on the first busy edge\n  hides setup without lengthening launch or adding an iteration.\n\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('first-digit table','first-digit fabric network')\ns=s.replace('first-four-bit divide table','first-four-bit fabric divider')\ns=s.replace('a 34-bit bank register and a small constant\\\\n  first-digit fabric network','a 34-bit bank register and a narrow\\\\n  first-digit fabric network')\ns=s.replace('using this same first-digit/preparation overlap.','using the same first-digit/preparation overlap, initially with a table.')\ns=s.replace('storage to reduce routing pressure while still shortening the divider.\\\\n  The large radix-16 measurement is negative evidence, not a claimed result\\\\n  for this smaller final implementation.', '''storage to reduce routing pressure while still shortening the divider.\n  A first two-step prototype using the ROM table reached only 58.245 MHz;\n  the critical source was that table's BSRAM DO pin. The final hypothesis\n  explicitly replaces the table with the four narrow fabric steps above.\n  These intermediate measurements are negative evidence, not results for\n  the final fabric implementation.''')\np.write_text(s)\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(s),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final fabric-prefix structure saved; schema valid.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
