{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r8s1.yaml');s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('fitness_delta_pct: 8','fitness_delta_pct: 5')\na=s.index('expected_impact:')\ns=s[:a]+'''  Final fabric-prefix prototype evidence: Gowin placement options 0/1/2\n  measured 67.169 / 66.653 / 66.653 MHz, median 66.653 MHz. It used\n  5,091 logic cells, 1,858 registers, zero LUT-RAM, four BSRAMs and six\n  DSPs. The first-digit ROM BSRAM is gone. Option zero's divider feedback\n  path is 20.180 ns and 63 cells, versus the champion's 21.382 ns and\n  130 cells. Ordinary WB-to-ALU now narrowly limits median timing. The\n  final prototype passed expanded real and ALTOPS ALU suites, and all\n  five cosimulation ELFs including stalled canonical CoreMark. These are\n  preliminary prototype measurements; independently repeat them during\n  implementation. The margin over the 4.6 percent threshold is small.\n\n  For reproducibility, first-prefix logic uses four statically generated\n  four-bit remainder/quotient pairs, five-bit trials and six-bit differences.\n  It shares the full-width divisor-high-zero predicate across all four\n  steps. triple_q is a 34-bit resettable flop updated only on busy iteration\n  zero. Each normal radix-4 step uses three parallel differences and a\n  four-term masked OR; the quotient bits use w2|w3 and w1|w3. Iteration\n  zero selects the prefix result; all other iterations select step two.\n  Keep both real and ALTOPS launch/control schedules unchanged. Prototype\n  research changes are restored after measurement; implement the described\n  structure and retain all existing checks.\n'''+s[a:]\np.write_text(s)\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nh=yaml.safe_load(s);jsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Measured final hypothesis saved; schema valid.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
