{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_22", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor s in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(s)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261002-001-r4s0':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis']);print(d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Make one local control-cone optimization: remove flush and redirect\nfrom the combinational instruction payload and from ID/EX payload\nwrite enables. Carry raw imem_data through IF/ID even on a killed or\nunavailable fetch, and implement bubbles at the ID/EX validity and\ncontrol boundary. Keep every pipeline stage, branch prediction policy,\ninstruction latency, divider schedule and external handshake intact.\n\nIn if_stage, drive out.instr directly from imem_data, retaining the\nexisting out.valid qualification and prediction metadata. Preserve\nreset and redirect priority in the PC update, including recovery\nwhile imemReady is low. Raw payload bits on an invalid bundle are\nirrelevant; the instruction must never acquire live controls.\n\nIn id_stage, separate payload capture from squash control. Reset\nretains its defined initialization. Otherwise capture pc, prediction,\noperands, immediate, register addresses and instruction whenever\n!stall, without qualifying this payload enable or zeroing these\nfields with flush, redirect or in.valid. For ctrl and valid only,\npreserve priority: reset clears; flush clears even if stall is also\nasserted; otherwise stall holds; otherwise a valid fetch captures\ndecoded controls and valid=1, and an invalid fetch captures ctrl='0\nand valid=0. A stalled instruction's full payload and controls remain\nstable. Clearing controls as well as valid is essential because the\nexisting memory, hazard and forwarding logic examines controls without\nuniversally gating them by validity. Do not change legal decoding or\nrely on valid alone to suppress writes, memory requests or forwarding.\n\nIn hazard_unit, compare the now-raw source fields for load-use, with\nimem_ready qualifying that dependency. Do not gate the source fields\nor dependency comparison with redirect, flush_if or out.valid: those\nwould reintroduce recovery into the operand-selection path. Recovery\nalready overrides PC hold, and flush_id already overrides ID/EX hold\nwhen EX advances. Preserve dmem and execute-wait hold priority and\nthe existing e\n…[1055 of 4127 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f44655db0d62a809]…\nn and retained 4,202,272 bracketed cycles\nfor ten iterations. The measured median Fmax and cycles imply fitness\n96.036, approximately 17.59 percent above the 81.67 champion. All 53\nchecks from the unchanged single-retirement formal configuration\npassed, including register consistency and liveness. These prototype\nresults do not replace final implementation verification.\n\nValidate with existing lint, pipeline tests, unchanged formal checks,\nand stalled RVFI cosimulation\nincluding canonical CoreMark CRCs, UART, address bounds and markers.\nAdd focused tests for killed raw stores, loads, divides and illegal\ninstructions, recovery coincident with imem stalls, and older dmem\nbackpressure, checking no wrong-path side effects, no duplicate\nretirement and stable held requests. Preserve nret=1 and all invariants.\nAcceptance requires fitness strictly above 85.42682, more than 4.6\npercent above 81.67; do not accept a gain inferred from logic depth\nalone. The same stall sequence should retain 4,202,272 CoreMark cycles.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\np=Path('cores/bench/generated/poison_probe/rtl');p.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nfor f in Path('cores/bench/rtl').glob('*.sv'):shutil.copyfile(f,p/f.name)\nf=p/'id_stage.sv';s=f.read_text()\ns=s.replace(\\\"    if (reset || flush) begin\\\\n      // Squash beats load-use hold. Raw wrong-path decode must never\\\\n      // leave active controls behind, even with validity cleared.\\\\n      reg_q <= '0;\\\\n    end else if (\"'!stall) begin\", \"    if (!stall) begin\")\ns=s.replace('\"'      reg_q.valid    <= in.valid;','')\ns=s.replace('  assign out = reg_q;', '''  logic live_q;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset || flush) live_q <= 1'b0;\n    else if (\"'!stall) live_q <= in.valid;\n  end\n  always_comb begin\n    out = reg_q;\n    out.valid = live_q;\n    out.ctrl.reg_write = reg_q.ctrl.reg_write && live_q;\n    out.ctrl.mem_read = reg_q.ctrl.mem_read && live_q;\n    out.ctrl.mem_write = reg_q.ctrl.mem_write && live_q;\n  end'\"''')\n# Avoid undriven/unused valid bit in packed raw register.\ns=s.replace('      reg_q.instr    <= in.instr;','      reg_q.instr    <= in.instr;\\\\n      reg_q.valid <= 1\\\\'b0;')\nf.write_text(s)\nprint('Wrote isolated validity-only recovery prototype')\nPY\nRTL_DIR=cores/bench/generated/poison_probe/rtl OBJ_DIR=cores/bench/generated/poison_probe/obj NRET=1 bash test/cosim/build.sh > cores/bench/generated/poison_probe/build.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
