{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '190,245p' test/cosim/main.cpp\"","aggregated_output":"                        uint8_t  mem_rmask, uint32_t mem_rdata,\n                        uint8_t  mem_wmask, uint32_t mem_wdata,\n                        uint8_t  trap, uint8_t halt, uint8_t intr,\n                        uint8_t  mode, uint8_t ixl) -> bool {\n            if (!v) return false;\n            char buf[640];\n            snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf),\n                \"{\\\"order\\\":%llu,\\\"cycle\\\":%llu,\\\"insn\\\":%u,\\\"pc_rdata\\\":%u,\\\"pc_wdata\\\":%u,\"\n                \"\\\"rd_addr\\\":%u,\\\"rd_wdata\\\":%u,\"\n                \"\\\"rs1_addr\\\":%u,\\\"rs1_rdata\\\":%u,\"\n                \"\\\"rs2_addr\\\":%u,\\\"rs2_rdata\\\":%u,\"\n                \"\\\"mem_addr\\\":%u,\\\"mem_rmask\\\":%u,\\\"mem_rdata\\\":%u,\"\n                \"\\\"mem_wmask\\\":%u,\\\"mem_wdata\\\":%u,\"\n                \"\\\"trap\\\":%u,\\\"halt\\\":%u,\\\"intr\\\":%u,\\\"mode\\\":%u,\\\"ixl\\\":%u}\",\n                (unsigned long long)order,\n                (unsigned long long)cycle,\n                insn, pc_rdata, pc_wdata,\n                rd_addr, rd_wdata,\n                rs1_addr, rs1_rdata,\n                rs2_addr, rs2_rdata,\n                mem_addr, mem_rmask, mem_rdata,\n                mem_wmask, mem_wdata,\n                (unsigned)trap, (unsigned)halt, (unsigned)intr,\n                (unsigned)mode, (unsigned)ixl);\n            if (bench_mode) {\n                strncpy(bench_last, buf, sizeof(bench_last)-1);\n                if (insn == 0x00100073) { hit_ebreak = true; return true; }\n            } else {\n                puts(buf);\n                fflush(stdout);\n                if (insn == 0x00100073) { hit_ebreak = true; return true; }\n            }\n            return false;\n        };\n\n        if (emit(top->io_rvfi_valid_0, top->io_rvfi_order_0, top->io_rvfi_insn_0,\n                 top->io_rvfi_pc_rdata_0, top->io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0,\n                 top->io_rvfi_rd_addr_0, top->io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0,\n                 top->io_rvfi_rs1_addr_0, top->io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_0,\n                 top->io_rvfi_rs2_addr_0, top->io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_0,\n                 top->io_rvfi_mem_addr_0,\n                 top->io_rvfi_mem_rmask_0, top->io_rvfi_mem_rdata_0,\n                 top->io_rvfi_mem_wmask_0, top->io_rvfi_mem_wdata_0,\n                 top->io_rvfi_trap_0, top->io_rvfi_halt_0, top->io_rvfi_intr_0,\n                 top->io_rvfi_mode_0, top->io_rvfi_ixl_0)) break;\n#if NRET >= 2\n        // Channel 1 — only present when the core is built with nret: 2.\n        // Cores declared nret: 1 expose no `_1` ports, so verilator's\n        // generated Vcore.h omits these fields and the build is keyed\n        // off the NRET macro injected by test/cosim/build.sh.\n        if (emit(top->io_rvfi_valid_1, top->io_rvfi_order_1, top->io_rvfi_insn_1,\n                 top->io_rvfi_pc_rdata_1, top->io_rvfi_pc_wdata_1,\n                 top->io_rvfi_rd_addr_1, top->io_rvfi_rd_wdata_1,\n                 top->io_rvfi_rs1_addr_1, top->io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_1,\n                 top->io_rvfi_rs2_addr_1, top->io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_1,\n                 top->io_rvfi_mem_addr_1,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  for k in ['motivation','hypothesis']:\n   s=h.get(k,'') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n   paragraphs=s.split('\\\\n\\\\n')\n   for p in paragraphs:\n    if any(x in p.lower() for x in ['replay','jalr frequency','return address','54,467','indirect count']): print(d['id'],k,p)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_18", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  for k in ['motivation','hypothesis']:\n   s=h.get(k,'') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n   paragraphs=s.split('\\\\n\\\\n')\n   for p in paragraphs:\n    if any(x in p.lower() for x in ['replay','jalr frequency','return address','54,467','indirect count']): print(d['id'],k,p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-003-r2s2 motivation The previous predictor hypothesis improved fitness to 13.38 by adding a\n128-entry bimodal table and early direct-JAL targets. Its measured critical\npath still runs through the execute ALU. A fresh trace of the unchanged\nchampion reproduces 4,202,272 bracketed CoreMark cycles and contains\n2,922,016 instructions, 529,588 conditional branches and only 13,735 JALRs.\nAn architectural branch-trace replay estimates 54,467 direction misses\nfor the existing bimodal table; a larger table saves only about 15,000.\nThese are replay estimates, not exact pipeline misprediction counters.\nBetter direction or return prediction alone has insufficient cycle-saving\nheadroom for the required 4.6 percent gain. The valuable unused capability\nof the existing predictor is producing a speculative fetch stream while\ndecode is blocked: today stall_if freezes the fetch PC on load-use and\ndata-memory stalls even when the instruction bus could deliver data.\n\nhyp-20261002-003-r2s2 hypothesis Extend the existing predictor into a bounded fetch-ahead engine with a\nfour-entry FIFO of predicted instructions. Retain the existing 128x2-bit\nbimodal direction table, legal direct-control-flow predecode, direct-target\ncalculation and EX comparison of actual_next_pc with predicted_next_pc.\nThe single architectural change is to let that predicted fetch stream\nadvance independently of decode backpressure while FIFO space remains.\nThis is a stream queue, with no instruction cache, address-based replay,\nnew direction predictor, return stack, or change to arithmetic latency.\nhyp-20261002-003-r3s2 motivation The champion already predicts direct JAL and conditional branches with a\n128-entry bimodal table. Prior branch-trace analysis found only about\n54,467 direction misses and 13,735 JALRs in 4,202,272 bracketed cycles,\ngiving direction-table or return-prediction changes too little headroom\nfor a reliable 4.6 percent gain. The predictor can instead supply useful\nfuture instructions while decode waits for a load-use hazard or dmem.\nhyp-20261002-003-r2s2 demonstrated 3,980,323 cycles with four predicted\ninstructions buffered, but its 5.567 MHz median on the old combinational\ndivider gave only 4.56 percent higher fitness and was rejected. The new\nchampion retains exactly 4,202,272 cycles, but its critical path is now\ninternal to the iterative divider and its area is much smaller. Revisit\nprediction-driven lookahead with a narrower queue to reduce the placement\npressure that erased the previous candidate's small acceptance margin.\n\nhyp-20261002-003-r6s2 motivation The champion stops its predicted instruction stream whenever decode\nwaits on execution or data memory. Earlier four-entry queues reduced\nCoreMark from 4,202,272 to 3,980,323 bracketed cycles, but did not beat\nthe contemporaneous winner. The current champion has a faster divider;\na smaller queue can expose those saved cycles with less added routing\nand state. Branch-trace replay found only 54,467 conditional direction\nmisses in 529,588 branches, versus 4.2 million cycles; enlarging the\ndirection table therefore offers too little cycle reduction by itself.\n\nhyp-20261002-003-r7s2 motivation The current core stops its predicted fetch stream whenever decode waits\nfor a load-use dependency, data memory or execution. Previous four- and\nthree-entry predictor queues saved about 5.3 percent of CoreMark cycles,\nbut their timing cost prevented them from replacing the winner. The new\nchampion has separated divide retirement and the physical memory address\nfrom general arithmetic. A smaller two-entry queue on this exact champion\npreserves most of the fetch overlap with only 102 payload bits and two\noccupancy bits. Direction-table growth alone offers little upside: the\nprior branch replay found only 54,467 conditional misses in 529,588 branches.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
