ting\n  stall_id supplies decode_hold. Return available = nonempty OR bus_ready\n  to hazard control in place of raw imemReady. Define consume = available\n  AND NOT decode_hold, pop = nonempty AND consume, and accept = bus_ready\n  AND (count < 2 OR pop), subject to the boundary r\n…[3643 of 6715 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:86da83b7766f6df4]…\ne internal\n      stall_if connection while preserving prediction training, recovery,\n      architectural interfaces, forwarding and retirement.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Interpret imem_ready as selected-instruction availability, including\n      buffered delivery during bus stalls. Remove the unused stall_if\n      output. Preserve load-use, dmem, execute-wait and squash priorities.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt predictor observations to distinguish raw responses from\n      accepted decode heads, preserving architectural assertions. Add\n      directed and randomized coverage of empty bypass, blocked\n      enqueue, every occupancy, simultaneous full pop/push, saved-token\n      stability during BHT training, recovery and reset. Cover load-use,\n      retained WB, divide holds, boundary bypass and wrong-path stores.\n      Check exact RVFI PCs, operands, order, single training/retirement,\n      no wrong-path memory effects and the existing liveness bound.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
