{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json cores/bench/LESSONS.md; rg -n 'predictor|r7s2|r8s2|bimodal|return.address|gshare' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r1s1 (broken, n/a): Budget iterative DIV/REM against the full retirement gap: eight iteration clocks plus launch/consume exhaust the 10-cycle RVFI liveness allowance, so a preceding load-use bubble stretches the gap to 11 cycles and fails liveness_ch0.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r1s2 (improvement, +10.40%): With combinational IF/ID, a 128-entry bimodal BHT and early JAL targets improve CoreMark by eliminating the single issue bubble on correctly predicted transfers, using EX comparison of actual_next_pc against the latched predicted_next_pc to flush only on misprediction.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r2s1 (improvement, +458.74%): Reusing eight restoring DIV/REM\n…[216139 of 219211 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:48c40fe135025cc1]…\ness\": 164.26, \"delta_pct\": 8.76, \"vs_baseline\": 1255.28, \"fmax_mhz\": 65.56, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3991298, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4886, \"ff\": 1928, \"seeds\": [63.33, 65.56, 65.56], \"perturbations\": [[0, 63.33, 24], [1, 65.56, 24], [2, 65.56, 24]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_4_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_13_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -10.79, \"arrival_ns\": 21.085, \"logic_cells\": 124, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 24, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T21:38:52.821421Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r8s2 (regression, +8.76%): On the fabric-register-file core, two fixed-head fetch entries preserve nearly all of a four-entry queue's stalled CoreMark cycle savings (~5%) with better prototype Fmax (64.234 versus 62.310 MHz), so queue depth must be chosen by throughput rather than cycles alone.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('\\\\nID:',d['id'],'TITLE:',d.get('title'),'OUTCOME:',d.get('outcome'),'FITNESS:',d.get('fitness'),'FMAX:',d.get('fmax_mhz'),'CYCLES:',d.get('cycles'))\n  print('MOTIVATION:',d.get('motivation',''))\n  if d['id'] not in ['hyp-20261002-003-r1s2','hyp-20261002-003-r8s2']:\n   print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  if d.get('implementation_notes'): print('NOTES:',d['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('\\\\nID:',d['id'],'TITLE:',d.get('title'),'OUTCOME:',d.get('outcome'),'FITNESS:',d.get('fitness'),'FMAX:',d.get('fmax_mhz'),'CYCLES:',d.get('cycles'))\n  print('MOTIVATION:',d.get('motivation',''))\n  if d['id'] not in ['hyp-20261002-003-r1s2','hyp-20261002-003-r8s2']:\n   print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  if d.get('implementation_notes'): print('NOTES:',d['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID: hyp-20261002-003-r1s2 TITLE: Early direct-control-flow prediction with a small bimodal table OUTCOME: improvement FITNESS: 13.38 FMAX: 5.623 CYCLES: 4202272\nMOTIVATION: The baseline predicts every control transfer sequentially and flushes on every\ntaken conditional branch, JAL, or JALR. Its IF/ID bundle is combinational, so a\ntaken transfer normally wastes one issue opportunity, not two. CoreMark's\nrepeated loops and direct calls should make many of these bubbles avoidable.\nThe only recorded experiment is the baseline; LESSONS.md is absent and there\nare no previous predictor results. The measured critical path is through\nforwarding and the combinational ALU, so this proposal targets iterations per\ncycle while keeping added prediction logic out of that arithmetic path.\n\n\nID: hyp-20261002-003-r2s2 TITLE: Prediction-driven fetch ahead across execute backpressure OUTCOME: regression FITNESS: 13.99 FMAX: 5.567 CYCLES: 3980323\nMOTIVATION: The previous predictor hypothesis improved fitness to 13.38 by adding a\n128-entry bimodal table and early direct-JAL targets. Its measured critical\npath still runs through the execute ALU. A fresh trace of the unchanged\nchampion reproduces 4,202,272 bracketed CoreMark cycles and contains\n2,922,016 instructions, 529,588 conditional branches and only 13,735 JALRs.\nAn architectural branch-trace replay estimates 54,467 direction misses\nfor the existing bimodal table; a larger table saves only about 15,000.\nThese are replay estimates, not exact pipeline misprediction counters.\nBetter direction or return prediction alone has insufficient cycle-saving\nheadroom for the required 4.6 percent gain. The valuable unused capability\nof the existing predictor is producing a speculative fetch stream while\ndecode is blocked: today stall_if freezes the fetch PC on load-use and\ndata-memory stalls even when the instruction bus could deliver data.\n\nPROPOSAL: Extend the existing predictor into a bounded fetch-ahead engine with a\nfour-entry FIFO of predicted instructions. Retain the existing 128x2-bit\nb\n…[36828 of 39900 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:069fb71fbbf7596a]…\nl hard invariants, including the ten-cycle ready-bus retirement bound.\nFinal fitness must exceed 134.2018 iterations/second, strictly more than\n4.6 percent above the champion; do not accept a cycle-only improvement.\n\n\nID: hyp-20261002-003-r8s2 TITLE: Two-entry predictor run-ahead on the fabric-register-file core OUTCOME: regression FITNESS: 164.26 FMAX: 65.56 CYCLES: 3991298\nMOTIVATION: Earlier predictor-stream queues reduced the canonical stalled CoreMark\ninterval from 4,202,272 to about 3,980,323 cycles, but lost to competing\ntiming improvements. Their last recorded critical path originated in\nthe old RAM register file and crossed execute recovery into fetch. The\ncurrent champion has removed that launch path with a fabric register\nfile and registered forwarding decisions; its limiting path is now\ninside the divider. This changes the timing case for a compact queue.\nPrior trace analysis found only 54,467 conditional misses and 13,735\nJALRs, so direction or return prediction alone has insufficient headroom.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
