k.\n\n  This is a timing hypothesis, not a demonstrated fitness improvement.\n  The champion's worst path also crosses writeback and multiplication;\n  that unchanged path may limit any benefit from reduced predictor fanout.\n  Closely spaced branches that alias in the BHT can suffer extra misses\n  from delayed training. Expect a modest Fmax improvement with little\n  cycle change, but confidence is low until vendor timing is measured.\n  At the existing 4,202,272-cycle count, acceptance requires median Fmax\n  above 74.333 MHz; recompute that threshold using the measured cycle\n  count if prediction timing changes it. Require fitness strictly above\n  176.88906 iterations/second, more than 4.6 percent above 169.11.\n\n  Validate an independent cycle-accurate delayed-training table model,\n  existing formal, real/ALTOPS unit tests, ready/stalled full-RVFI cosim\n  and canonical stalled CoreMark. Preserve all canonical CRCs, UART text,\n  address bounds, timing markers and retirement-liveness checks. Measure\n  all three Gowin placement options on the eventual implementation.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a resettable valid/index/outcome event register between existing\n      EX branch-training inputs and the local BHT counter writes. Drain one\n      pending event and accept the next on each edge. Retain all prediction,\n      PC-update, target guards, saturation and counter-reset behavior;\n      introduce no training-to-prediction bypass or fetch queue.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Model the one-clock training delay explicitly, keeping all architectural\n      and saved-token recovery assertions. Test consecutive same-index and\n      different-index events, saturation, pending-event drain during imem,\n      dmem and divide holds, reset cancellation, recovery and no duplicate\n      updates. Adapt exact prediction-sequence expectations against an\n      independent delayed-table model rather than deleting them. Preserve\n      legal-branch-only event checks, wrong-path side-effect checks, RVFI\n      PC/order/operand checks and all existing liveness and arithmetic tests.\n''')\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Revised hypothesis schema valid')\nprint('Exact unchanged-cycle threshold MHz:',176.88906*4202272/1e7)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Revised hypothesis schema valid\nExact unchanged-cycle threshold MHz: 74.333594394432\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
