sume the dividend from most-significant\nto least-significant two-bit groups in sixteen combinational steps.\nEach step forms T = 4*R + next_pair and calculates T-D, T-2D and T-3D\nin parallel. Select the highest non-borrowing candidate, giving quotient\ndigit 3, 2, 1 or 0 and the associated next remainder. Do not implement\nthis as three serial compare/subtract operations or derive the remainder\nby multiplying a quotient back by the divisor.\n\nStatically taper the trial arithmetic: after processing W dividend bits,\nT fits in W bits, with W = 2, 4, ..., 32. For each divisor multiple M,\ncalculate a W+1-bit unsigned difference between zero-extended T and\nM[W-1:0]. A candidate is eligible only when its borrow bit is clear AND\nM[33:W] is zero. This high-bit guard is essential; truncating a large\ndivisor multiple must never make it appear subtractable. Use constant\ngenerate widths so synthesis sees three pa\n…[41286 of 44358 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9b5b75dac5b3b7f9]…\n 176.88906 iter/s, more than 4.6 percent above 169.11,\ncorresponding to approximately 74.334 MHz at the unchanged cycle count.\nDo not change evaluator, benchmark, formal or interface contracts.\n\nPreliminary exploration is negative evidence about nearby alternatives,\nnot a measured claim for this final circuit: preselected WB with flat\nEX operand masks and the original multipliers reached 70.146 MHz.\nAdding the shared multiplier to that flat-mux variant reached 73.606\nMHz, about 3.6 percent above the champion and below acceptance. It used\n5,043 logic cells, 1,825 registers, zero LUT-RAM, four BSRAMs and two\nDSPs; all 53 standard formal checks, 13 ALU/pipeline configurations,\nselftest and canonical CoreMark passed. Registering divide ownership\nin that variant made timing worse and is excluded. The proposed final\ncircuit retains the original EX operand muxes and opcode decoding to\navoid those additional routing changes. Final measurements must be\nreproduced by the implementation phase before acceptance.\n\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
