{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_70", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r10s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Shorten the branch decision-to-counter update cone'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 177.89 iter/s at 75.4 MHz with 4,238,604 marked CoreMark cycles. Its worst path crosses EX recovery/control. Temporary local timing experiments expose two coupled costs in the same branch-outcome cone: full-width branch ordering comparison and outcome-dependent updates of 128 saturating counters. Parallel byte comparison alone measured 74.995 MHz and exposed counter-update paths; Gray-coded counters alone measured 70.637 MHz and exposed a 43-cell operand-to-recovery path. Neither isolated edit clears acceptance. Target this one combinational decision-and-update cone together while preserving every prediction and cycle boundary. Prior delayed-training predictor work regressed, so do not change predictor policy or training latency.'''\nprefix='''Optimize the existing branch decision-to-counter-update cone with a balanced byte comparator feeding minimal Gray-coded saturating-counter updates. These are complementary local logic changes on the same timed control path. Add no pipeline stage, change no prediction algorithm, and preserve every instruction latency and training edge.\n\nIn ex_stage.sv, compute four parallel pairs E[j]=(rs1[8*j+:8]==rs2[8*j+:8]) and L[j]=(rs1[8*j+:8]<rs2[8*j+:8]) for j=0..3. Combine bytes 3/2 and 1/0 in parallel using E_pair=E_hi && E_lo and L_pair=L_hi || (E_hi && L_lo), then combine those two groups with the same rule. Use explicit balanced wires, not a serial priority loop or a 32-bit subtraction. The root E and L are full-word equality and unsigned_less. signed_less=(rs1[31] XOR rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : unsigned_less. Feed the unchanged branch-op case with equality/inequality, signed less/not-less and unsigned less/not-less; retain default false for reserved branch operations. Preserve forwarded operand muxes, targets, alignment checks, direction-token recovery and branch_update qualification. Leave ALU SLT/SLTU and all M arithmetic unchanged.\n\n'''\nd['hypothesis']=prefix+d['hypothesis'].replace('Make one micro_opt change: Gray-encode','In if_stage.sv, Gray-encode').replace('Preserve all operand, recovery, forwarding, ALU, divider, memory and RVFI logic.','Preserve all other operand, recovery, forwarding, ALU, divider, memory and RVFI logic.').replace('The intended gain is shorter and smaller counter-update logic on the late branch-outcome path','The intended gain is shorter ordering comparison followed by smaller counter-update logic on the same late branch-outcome path')\nd['hypothesis']+='''\\\\n\\\\nValidate comparator equality, unsigned ordering and signed ordering against independent full-width comparisons for arbitrary 32-bit operands, using a combinational equivalence miter when available. Include most-significant differing bytes, opposite signs, equality, extreme operands and both EX/WB forwarding sources in branch tests. The isolated comparator passed such a SAT miter, all existing pipeline configurations, all 53 standard formal checks and canonical CoreMark validation. The isolated Gray-counter variant passed the added prediction-sequence test, all 11 pipeline configurations, all 53 standard formal checks and canonical CoreMark at exactly 4,238,604 cycles. Those isolated checks do not establish the combined circuit's final timing or acceptance. Standard formal uses ALTOPS; this proposal leaves real M arithmetic unchanged.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes'].insert(0,{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace only branch equality and ordering comparisons with four parallel byte E/L comparisons and an explicit two-level balanced lexicographic tree. Derive signed_less from signs and unsigned_less and retain the existing six-way branch case and default. Keep all operand sources, targets, alignment/recovery conditions and pipeline state unchanged.'''})\nd['changes'][-1]['description']+=' Also cover all branch conditions, each most-significant differing byte, opposite signs and forwarding sources against independent full-width comparisons; preserve all existing assertions.'\nclass LiteralDumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef rep(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data or len(data)>120 else None)\nLiteralDumper.add_representer(str,rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=LiteralDumper,sort_keys=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final combined proposal schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
