\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep4/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-001-r10s0-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p2/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\nscore Fmax (median): 68.764 MHz\n...........                                                              [100%]\n11 passed in 75.62s (0:01:15)\nSBY  0:54:54 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\nSBY  0:54:54 [reg_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\n\nFormal: 53 passed, 0 failed\npython3 -m tools.eval.cosim . bench\n{\n  \"passed\": true,\n  \"elfs_tested\": 2\n}\n{\"ebreak\":true,\"maxcycles_hit\":false,\"oob\":false,\"bench_start_cycle\":14996,\"bench_stop_cycle\":4253600,\"bench_bracketed\":true,\"uart\":\"2K performance run parameters\n…[7977 of 11049 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c259c37618d160a0]…\nep all operand sources, targets, alignment/recovery conditions and pipeline state unchanged.\n- file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n  description: |-\n    Replace the generated counters' conditional binary increment/decrement and saturation holds with Gray encoding SN=00, WN=01, WT=11, ST=10. On the unchanged entry-qualified training edge assign high_next=low ? branch_taken : high and low_next=high XOR branch_taken. Keep reset=01, high-bit prediction, table shape, all PC logic and same-cycle training.\n- file: test/test_pipeline.py\n  description: |-\n    Extend the IF-stage counter checks with exhaustive four-state/two-outcome transitions using an independent saturating-integer reference, reset and unselected holds. Preserve existing same-index read-before-write, alias, saturation, prediction-token, recovery and stalled full-core assertions. Also cover all branch conditions, each most-significant differing byte, opposite signs and forwarding sources against independent full-width comparisons; preserve all existing assertions.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"agent_message","text":"The combined prototype also misses the threshold at 68.764 MHz, despite passing correctness checks. I’ll exclude counter recoding from the submitted hypothesis and narrow it to a refined branch comparator: four-bit comparison groups plus factored condition selection. Its performance remains unmeasured, so the proposal will retain low confidence and document the negative timing evidence."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_74", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cp /srv/hwebench/tmp/92f133a1/f880d9f8/r10s0-if_stage.original.sv cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv; cp /srv/hwebench/tmp/92f133a1/f880d9f8/r10s0-ex_stage.original.sv cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv; cp /srv/hwebench/tmp/92f133a1/f880d9f8/r10s0-test_pipeline.original.py cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py; python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema,textwrap\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r10s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-001-r10s0',\n'title':'Four-bit branch comparison tree with factored condition selection',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 177.89 iter/s at 75.4 MHz with 4,238,604 marked CoreMark cycles. Its recorded worst path runs from an ID/EX operand through EX recovery into forwarding-selector control. Prior micro_opt attempts focused on arithmetic and operand delivery; the latest MEM-multiply champion exposes control resolution. Local experiments show full-width branch ordering comparison on deep operand-to-recovery paths. Target the comparator and its trailing condition mux as one local Boolean-mapping problem, preserving pipeline and prediction behavior.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only EX branch condition generation with a balanced tree of eight parallel unsigned four-bit comparisons, followed by a factored condition selector. This is one micro_opt of the branch decision cone. Keep forwarded operands, target adders, alignment handling, direction-token recovery, BHT state/encoding/training, squash rules and all instruction latencies unchanged. Do not change ALU SLT/SLTU, multiplication, division or any pipeline boundary.\n\nFor nibble j=0..7, compute E[j]=(rs1[4*j+:4]==rs2[4*j+:4]) and L[j]=(rs1[4*j+:4]<rs2[4*j+:4]) in parallel. Combine adjacent high/low groups using E=E_hi AND E_lo and L=L_hi OR (E_hi AND L_lo). Build exactly three balanced levels: eight nibbles to four bytes, four bytes to two halfwords, then one word. Use explicit named wires or a constant-index generate tree, not a serial priority accumulator. Root E is equality and root L is unsigned_less. Four-bit groups bound each local carry chain and fit the target FPGA's small logic cells; measure the extra tree level against that reduction.\n\nFactor the final six-condition case into the RV32 branch funct3 bits, avoiding separate signed/unsigned comparators and duplicated inverted condition selection. Let f=in.ctrl.branch_op and signs_differ=rs1[31] XOR rs2[31]. Compute ordered_less = signs_differ ? (rs1[31] XOR f[1]) : unsigned_less. For ordering branches, f[1]=0 selects signed and f[1]=1 selects unsigned. Compute selected = f[2] ? ordered_less : equal, then branch_cond = (f[2] OR \"'!f[1]) AND (selected XOR f[0]). This implements BEQ/BNE for f=0/1, signed BLT/BGE for f=4/5, unsigned BLTU/BGEU for f=6/7, and exactly false for reserved f=2/3. Preserve this default behavior even in stage-local tests that drive otherwise illegal controls. These factored equations are part of the proposal, not merely changing comparison group width.\n\nThe intended gain is fewer dependent carry and mux levels between forwarded operands and branch outcome/recovery, without a cycle, prediction, or throughput penalty. Do not alter branch_update qualifications or move training in time. Preserve nret=1, trap-cancelled writes, held WB forwarding, memory handshakes, decoder legality, exact RVFI order and the ten-cycle liveness limit. The original table and all M-extension arithmetic remain intact.\n\nValidate the complete branch_cond function against the original full-width case for arbitrary two 32-bit operands and all eight funct3 values, preferably with a combinational SAT equivalence miter. Test equality, opposite signs, signed extrema, every most-significant differing nibble, lower nibbles that disagree with the winning high nibble, and both EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding sources. Retain existing recovery-token equivalence, reserved/misaligned branch, predictor, load/multiply-use, dmem-hold, imem-stall and exact retirement assertions. Run lint, real/ALTOPS pipeline tests, unchanged formal, full-RVFI ready/stalled selftest and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/address/marker checks.\n\nEvidence and limits: a temporary four-BYTE comparator retaining the original branch-op case was correct by SAT, all 53 standard formal checks, existing pipeline tests and CoreMark, but measured only 74.995 MHz median. Isolated payload/squash separation reached 72.94 MHz. Counter Boolean rewriting and Gray recoding also regressed; combining byte comparison with Gray counters reached 68.764 MHz despite passing all 53 formal checks, 11 pipeline configurations and canonical CoreMark. Those variants are excluded. The final proposal uses four-BIT groups and explicitly factored sign/condition selection, with the original predictor unchanged. Its full vendor timing has not been measured, and no earlier prototype result is claimed as its performance. Confidence is low because divider or remaining branch fanout may limit the gain.\n\nExpect the same 4,238,604 bracketed CoreMark cycles for the same bus-stall sequence. Acceptance requires measured median Gowin Fmax times actual iterations/cycle strictly above 186.07294 iter/s, more than 4.6 percent above 177.89; about 78.869 MHz is needed at unchanged cycles. Report the actual score and critical paths rather than assuming that shorter local arithmetic guarantees acceptance. All temporary RTL and test edits from exploration are restored; this file is the implementation proposal.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace only branch condition generation with eight parallel four-bit equality/unsigned-less comparisons, three balanced lexicographic combine levels, and the specified factored funct3/sign/inversion equations. Keep reserved conditions false and preserve every target, alignment, update, recovery, forwarding and pipeline control.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Extend independent-reference branch-condition tests across all eight funct3 values, each winning nibble, equality, signed boundaries, opposite signs, lower-nibble conflicts and both forwarded operands. Preserve existing token, predictor, trap, bus-hold, liveness and retirement checks. Verify the complete factored function against original full-width comparisons, including reserved-operation defaults.'''}]}\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef represent(dumper,s):\n if len(s)>120:\n  s='\\\\n\\\\n'.join(textwrap.fill(part,76) for part in s.split('\\\\n\\\\n'))+'\\\\n'\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nD.add_representer(str,represent)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261003-001-r10s0'\nprint('Final hypothesis schema valid:',p)\nPY\ngit status --short\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
