.ctrl.is_jalr ? indirect_recovery_target : direct_recovery_target.\n  Keep actual_next_pc and its EX/MEM capture unchanged for every instruction,\n  including correctly predicted branches, normal instructions and traps.\n\n  The direct identity is required only when redirect is asse\n…[3349 of 6421 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9a9620a4e2b23709]…\ns. Other close paths make this a low-confidence estimate.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive direct recovery target selection from frozen predicted_direct,\n      and separately preserve JALR aligned-sum versus trap-fall-through\n      selection. Select the two with is_jalr. Keep architectural actual_next_pc,\n      redirect enable, comparator, training, traps, owners and all registers\n      and instruction latencies unchanged.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check target equivalence to architectural actual_next_pc on every\n      asserted redirect and retain architectural-PC checks on all retirements.\n      Extend direct-token and JALR coverage across range/alignment/wrap,\n      forwarding and bus-hold cases. Adapt only assumptions that the unused\n      recovery bus must equal the architectural next PC when redirect is low;\n      preserve all architectural, side-effect, trap and liveness assertions.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
