d T and\nM[W-1:0]. A candidate is eligible only when its borrow bit is clear AND\nM[33:W] is zero. This high-bit guard is essential; truncating a large\ndivisor multiple must never make it appear subtractable. Use constant\ngenerate widths so synthesis sees three parallel narrow subtractors per\nstep, rather than a chain of full-width comparisons and subtraction.\n\nRestore quotient sign with sign(a) XOR sign(b) for signed operations;\nrestore remainder sign from sign(a) alone. Explicitly preserve quotient\n0xffffffff and remainder a for division by zero, and quotient 0x80000000\nand remainder zero for signed INT_MIN/-1. Keep the existing per-operation\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas unchanged and excl\n…[45006 of 48078 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c859ae0aba0be09b]…\n existing ALU operand forwarding, EX/MEM and MEM/WB boundaries,\nmultiply and divide implementations and protocols, branch predictor,\nregister-file storage, memory interfaces and nret=1 unchanged. Preserve\nall decoder legality, trap, RVFI ordering and liveness checks. Identical\ninstruction results and latencies should preserve exactly 4,238,604\nmarker-bracketed CoreMark cycles under the standard stall sequence.\n\nProve combinational equivalence of all three shift results against the\noriginal native expressions for arbitrary a and b. Test all 32 shift\ndistances with zero, all ones, signed e\nPATH: {'from': 'cpu/u_fwd/fwd_rs1_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/pc_18_s1', 'slack_ns': -8.729, 'arrival_ns': 19.024, 'logic_cells': 42, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']}\nhyp-20261003-002-r13s1 structural Eight-cycle divider with width-specialized radix scheduling 74.12 -10.58\nhyp-20261003-003-r13s2 predictor PC-only direct-target prediction with decode-time stale-entry recovery 69.053 -17.02\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
