{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Drive direct divide retirement from its registered completion token'\nd['motivation']='''The current direct divide retirement grant redundantly depends on the held instruction's decoded divide opcode and general EX advance expression. That grant controls the full retirement bundle mux and therefore the register-file write-first operand path. Timing probes expose paths from ID/EX alu_op through this completion selection into ID operands. Structural r11s1 and r13s1 included a div_done-based grant together with large divider rewrites, so their regressions do not isolate this local control simplification. The original eight-cycle divider can be preserved while removing live opcode decoding from the retirement grant.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Make one local completion-control simplification in ex_stage.sv: replace div_consume = is_divide && advance with div_consume = div_done && \"'!normal_wb_valid && !stall && !reset. Keep div_completion.valid driven by div_consume. Preserve all other assignments, including is_divide, div_request, execute_wait, advance, divider busy/done state, launch operand snapshots and completion metadata.\n\nThe registered div_done bit is the ownership certificate. It can become set only after a valid divide launches, and ID/EX retains that instruction until completion is consumed. While the divider is busy or completion waits for older WB, execute_wait holds ID/EX and blocks younger issue. Older dmem holds retain ID/EX and defer launch or consumption. Reset clears done and the new grant explicitly gates reset. An advancing divide cannot redirect or trigger its own load/multiply-use bubble. Thus reachable div_done implies a valid matching held divide, and the removed is_divide/advance terms do not change any retirement edge.\n\nProve that ownership implication; do not assume an arbitrary ALU done token is enough without validating integration. When div_done is high, assert ID/EX.valid and that its legal decoded ALU operation is one of DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, with the original instruction and metadata still owned by the request. Under that reachable-state invariant, prove the new grant equals the old is_divide && advance expression. Preserve oldest-first retirement by retaining !normal_wb_valid, and retain !stall and !reset even if some combinations are currently unreachable. Clear done only through the existing consume protocol. Keep exactly one retirement pulse and the unchanged eight iteration clocks and fixed liveness limit.\n\nThis removes redundant live opcode/valid/general-advance logic from the 32-bit divide-versus-normal retirement mux and its register-file write-first path. The normal WB forwarding data must remain directly connected to retained mem_wb_w.alu_result; do not add direct divide completion to EX forwarding. Snapshot divide operands only on the original request edge, retain all result/sign/exception logic, and preserve write enable, rd, x0 behavior, RVFI fields and sequential order. All ALTOPS formulas and real M-extension arithmetic remain unchanged.\n\nNo arithmetic rewrite, early divide completion, new state, retimed recovery, forwarding encoding, branch-prediction change, pipeline stage or interface modification belongs to this hypothesis. Keep nret=1 and every decoder legality, trap, memory and benchmark invariant. This is a micro_opt of one redundant control cone, not the wider structural divider designs used in r11s1/r13s1.\n\nThe expected benefit is shorter completion-select fanout into register-file reads and ID/EX operand capture, with no cycle-count change. This may expose an unchanged divider or branch path, and synthesis may already simplify some redundant terms. A gain must be established by vendor timing; low confidence is appropriate for this small change.\n\nExtend integration tests to assert divide ownership throughout busy/done, exact equality of old and new grants in every reached cycle, stable metadata until consume, older-WB priority, reset cancellation and exactly-once retirement. Exercise both forwarded operands, load-to-divide, back-to-back divides, direct completion to a younger consumer, wrong-path divides, imem stalls and long older dmem holds. Retain real and ALTOPS suites and every existing RVFI, arithmetic and liveness assertion. Standalone EX tests must obey and separately check the launch/hold protocol; do not mask impossible ownership violations.\n\nRun unchanged nret=1 formal, ready/stalled full-RVFI cosimulation and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/address/marker checks. Preserve all existing contracts. CoreMark should retain 4,238,604 bracketed cycles under the standard stall sequence. Measure all three Gowin options and actual iterations/cycle; acceptance requires fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s, more than 4.6 percent above 195.55, or approximately 86.699 MHz median at unchanged cycles.\n\nOther session probes are rejected and excluded: registered one-hot forwarding passed ten pipeline configurations but measured 63.286 MHz median; speculative add-before-forwarding address generation passed ten configurations and an algebraic SAT miter but measured 72.138 MHz median. Start this change from the champion'\"'s unmodified binary forwarding, original address arithmetic and original divider. Those results are negative evidence about those alternatives, not measurements of the final completion-grant proposal.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Derive div_consume solely from registered div_done and unchanged older-WB, dmem-stall and reset guards. Preserve all launch, hold, arithmetic, completion-bundle, forwarding and retirement behavior.'},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add ownership and old/new consumption-grant equivalence assertions over reachable cycles, with stable metadata, reset, held completion, dependency, stalled older memory and exactly-once RVFI coverage. Keep all existing real/ALTOPS, arithmetic, trap and liveness checks.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=82))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated and validated completion-grant proposal')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
