{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_46", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Byte-parallel carry-select addition for forwarded effective addresses'\nd['motivation']='''Recent micro_opt r11s0 and r13s0 timing paths start at forwarding selector registers and traverse EX into fetch-PC recovery. The champion removed JALR target arithmetic from recovery enable, but its target data still depends on a forwarded base plus a 32-bit immediate. A local adder topology change targets that remaining carry path without adding recovery bubbles. The failed branch-comparator and shared-shifter experiments motivate restricting this change to the shared load/store/JALR base-plus-immediate adder.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace only the rs1-plus-immediate effective-address adder in ex_stage.sv with four parallel eight-bit carry-select blocks and an explicit block carry-lookahead network. Reuse its result for effective_addr and jalr_sum. Keep the existing binary source forwarding mux before this adder, all raw operand paths and every pipeline register unchanged.\n\nFor byte k=0..3 of the forwarded rs1 value A and immediate B, compute Z[k] = {0,A_byte}+{0,B_byte} in nine unsigned bits and O[k] = A_byte+B_byte+1 in eight bits, independently of the actual incoming carry. G[k]=Z[k][8] and P[k]=AND-reduction(A_byte XOR B_byte). Define c0=0, c1=G0, c2=G1 OR (P1 AND G0), and c3=G2 OR (P2 AND G1) OR (P2 AND P1 AND G0). Output byte zero is Z0[7:0]; bytes one through three select O[k] if c[k] else Z[k][7:0]. Generate only the used propagate/generate signals. Express carries as these parallel Boolean equations, not as a serial loop that propagates carry through all four byte adders. Discard the final carry-out, preserving exact modulo-2\"'^32 addition.\n\nThe intended physical topology is short independent byte additions, a shallow block-carry network and final byte selection. O[k] must not depend on the real incoming carry. Gowin may share the two local sum candidates or use carry resources for the increment; inspect the mapped depth rather than assuming the source shape guarantees speed. This avoids the three full base-plus-immediate adders of speculative add-before-forwarding, while shortening the remaining single selected-base carry chain.\n\nUse the full 32-bit selected result for the byte effective address. JALR clears result bit zero only after addition; it still checks bit one, traps on misalignment, suppresses the link write and falls through exactly as before. Preserve unconditional recovery for every advancing legal JALR, including target equal to PC+4. Leave the direct branch/JAL PC-plus-immediate adder, PC increment, general ALU ADD/SUB, branch comparisons, multiplier and divider unchanged. No arithmetic may be truncated to the benchmark address range.\n\nRetain exact EX/MEM effective-address gating and all MEM byte lanes, width checks, misalignment traps and side-effect suppression. The source mux keeps EX-over-WB-over-local priority, x0 and retained ordinary WB semantics across dmem stalls. Preserve divider snapshots, direct retirement, register-file write-first reads, all hazard/flush priorities, BHT behavior and nret=1. No new stage, instruction latency, prediction policy, forwarding encoding or completion-grant rewrite is included.\n\nProve the complete 32-bit adder equivalent to native A+B for arbitrary operands. Exercise carries across every byte boundary, full carry propagation, alternating propagate/generate/kill bytes, signed offsets, wraparound and all low-bit alignments. Check local, EX and retained-WB address sources for loads, stores and JALR, both matching owners, load/multiply-use bubbles, long dmem holds, reset, wrong-path cancellation, JALR bit-zero clearing and trap/link suppression. Preserve every existing real/ALTOPS, architectural, memory, RVFI and fixed-liveness assertion.\n\nRun strict lint, pipeline suites, unchanged formal, ready/stalled full-RVFI cosimulation and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/address/marker validation. Identical arithmetic and cycle boundaries should preserve 4,238,604 bracketed CoreMark cycles for the standard stall sequence. Measure all three Gowin options and actual cycles. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s, more than 4.6 percent above 195.55, corresponding to approximately 86.699 MHz median at unchanged cycles.\n\nThe gain remains uncertain: extra byte-sum logic and final mux routing may offset the shorter carry path, and fetch/branch/divider paths can cap Fmax. Earlier independent probes in this session were negative: one-hot forwarding reached 63.286 MHz median, three speculative address sums reached 72.138 MHz, and a div_done-only consumption grant reached 68.326 MHz. Each passed ten pipeline configurations, but none is included here. This proposal starts from the unchanged champion and changes only the address-adder implementation.'\"'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Implement the selected-base-plus-immediate sum with four eight-bit parallel carry-select blocks and explicit block carry-lookahead; share its exact 32-bit result between effective_addr and jalr_sum. Preserve original forwarding, final target/trap logic, every pipeline boundary and all other arithmetic.'},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add independent native-addition reference checks over carry boundaries, arbitrary operands, forwarding sources, address alignment and wraparound, plus held-memory and JALR integration cases. Retain every existing architectural, real/ALTOPS, RVFI, side-effect and liveness assertion.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=82))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Validated carry-select proposal')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_46", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Byte-parallel carry-select addition for forwarded effective addresses'\nd['motivation']='''Recent micro_opt r11s0 and r13s0 timing paths start at forwarding selector registers and traverse EX into fetch-PC recovery. The champion removed JALR target arithmetic from recovery enable, but its target data still depends on a forwarded base plus a 32-bit immediate. A local adder topology change targets that remaining carry path without adding recovery bubbles. The failed branch-comparator and shared-shifter experiments motivate restricting this change to the shared load/store/JALR base-plus-immediate adder.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace only the rs1-plus-immediate effective-address adder in ex_stage.sv with four parallel eight-bit carry-select blocks and an explicit block carry-lookahead network. Reuse its result for effective_addr and jalr_sum. Keep the existing binary source forwarding mux before this adder, all raw operand paths and every pipeline register unchanged.\n\nFor byte k=0..3 of the forwarded rs1 value A and immediate B, compute Z[k] = {0,A_byte}+{0,B_byte} in nine unsigned bits and O[k] = A_byte+B_byte+1 in eight bits, independently of the actual incoming carry. G[k]=Z[k][8] and P[k]=AND-reduction(A_byte XOR B_byte). Define c0=0, c1=G0, c2=G1 OR (P1 AND G0), and c3=G2 OR (P2 AND G1) OR (P2 AND P1 AND G0). Output byte zero is Z0[7:0]; bytes one through three select O[k] if c[k] else Z[k][7:0]. Generate only the used propagate/generate signals. Express carries as these parallel Boolean equations, not as a serial loop that propagates carry through all four byte adders. Discard the final carry-out, preserving exact modulo-2\"'^32 addition.\n\nThe intended physical topology is short independent byte additions, a shallow block-carry network and final byte selection. O[k] must not depend on the real incoming carry. Gowin may share the two local sum candidates or use carry resources for the increment; inspect the mapped depth rather than assuming the source shape guarantees speed. This avoids the three full base-plus-immediate adders of speculative add-before-forwarding, while shortening the remaining single selected-base carry chain.\n\nUse the full 32-bit selected result for the byte effective address. JALR clears result bit zero only after addition; it still checks bit one, traps on misalignment, suppresses the link write and falls through exactly as before. Preserve unconditional recovery for every advancing legal JALR, including target equal to PC+4. Leave the direct branch/JAL PC-plus-immediate adder, PC increment, general ALU ADD/SUB, branch comparisons, multiplier and divider unchanged. No arithmetic may be truncated to the benchmark address range.\n\nRetain exact EX/MEM effective-address gating and all MEM byte lanes, width checks, misalignment traps and side-effect suppression. The source mux keeps EX-over-WB-over-local priority, x0 and retained ordinary WB semantics across dmem stalls. Preserve divider snapshots, direct retirement, register-file write-first reads, all hazard/flush priorities, BHT behavior and nret=1. No new stage, instruction latency, prediction policy, forwarding encoding or completion-grant rewrite is included.\n\nProve the complete 32-bit adder equivalent to native A+B for arbitrary operands. Exercise carries across every byte boundary, full carry propagation, alternating propagate/generate/kill bytes, signed offsets, wraparound and all low-bit alignments. Check local, EX and retained-WB address sources for loads, stores and JALR, both matching owners, load/multiply-use bubbles, long dmem holds, reset, wrong-path cancellation, JALR bit-zero clearing and trap/link suppression. Preserve every existing real/ALTOPS, architectural, memory, RVFI and fixed-liveness assertion.\n\nRun strict lint, pipeline suites, unchanged formal, ready/stalled full-RVFI cosimulation and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/address/marker validation. Identical arithmetic and cycle boundaries should preserve 4,238,604 bracketed CoreMark cycles for the standard stall sequence. Measure all three Gowin options and actual cycles. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s, more than 4.6 percent above 195.55, corresponding to approximately 86.699 MHz median at unchanged cycles.\n\nThe gain remains uncertain: extra byte-sum logic and final mux routing may offset the shorter carry path, and fetch/branch/divider paths can cap Fmax. Earlier independent probes in this session were negative: one-hot forwarding reached 63.286 MHz median, three speculative address sums reached 72.138 MHz, and a div_done-only consumption grant reached 68.326 MHz. Each passed ten pipeline configurations, but none is included here. This proposal starts from the unchanged champion and changes only the address-adder implementation.'\"'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Implement the selected-base-plus-immediate sum with four eight-bit parallel carry-select blocks and explicit block carry-lookahead; share its exact 32-bit result between effective_addr and jalr_sum. Preserve original forwarding, final target/trap logic, every pipeline boundary and all other arithmetic.'},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add independent native-addition reference checks over carry boundaries, arbitrary operands, forwarding sources, address alignment and wraparound, plus held-memory and JALR integration cases. Retain every existing architectural, real/ALTOPS, RVFI, side-effect and liveness assertion.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=82))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Validated carry-select proposal')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Validated carry-select proposal\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
