 ns, 10 cells, cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_5_s1 -> cpu/u_rf/g_word[18].word_q_29_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep4/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p1/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\nplace_option 2: Fmax 72.739 MHz, 11 logic levels; logic 5155, registers 1832, LUT-RAM 0, BSRAM 4, DSP 6\n  path 1: 19.042 ns, 13 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_1_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_7_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_id > cpu > cpu/u_rf\n  path 2: 19.04 ns, 34 cells, cpu/u_fwd/fwd_rs1_0_s0 -> cpu/u_if/pc_9_s1\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_if\n  path 3: 19.037 ns, 63 cells, cpu/u_ex/u_alu/divisor_q_6_s0 -> cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_3_s1\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex/u_alu\n  path 4: 19.036 ns, 10 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_1_s0 -> cpu/u_rf/g_word[23].word_q_14_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_id > cpu > cpu/u_rf\n  path 5: 18.988 ns, 10 cells, cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_5_s1 -> cpu/u_rf/g_word[18].word_q_29_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep4/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p2/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\nscore Fmax (median): 72.739 MHz\n02:10:15\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-001-r14s0',\n'title':'Prune the unused divide-to-EX/MEM ALU result route',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion retires DIV/REM directly from the dedicated div_result output and inserts an EX/MEM bubble on every divide edge, including consumption. However, alu.sv also selects div_result onto its ordinary combinational out bus for all four divide opcodes. That bus feeds the normal EX/MEM result cone even though no dividing instruction can capture it there. Removing this redundant result route can reduce divider-result fanout and ordinary ALU output selection without modifying arithmetic, instruction latency or any valid retirement. Recent micro_opt branch-comparator, register-file and shifter rewrites regressed; this proposal instead specializes an already separate completion interface.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Introduce a default-enabled ALU parameter named ENABLE_DIVIDE_OUT. In the ALU output case, DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU return div_result when this parameter is true and 32'b0 when false. Instantiate the EX-stage ALU with ENABLE_DIVIDE_OUT=0 alongside its existing ENABLE_MULTIPLY=0. Preserve the dedicated div_result output, divider state machine, request/busy/done/consume handshake, magnitude and sign handling, special cases and exact eight busy clocks. The parameter affects only the ordinary combinational out bus, never the actual divide completion output.\n\nThe standalone ALU defaults to the original behavior, including divide values on out for existing arithmetic tests. Apply the same output-route specialization in real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS builds, without changing any ALTOPS formula, constant or handshake. All non-divide output case arms, including defaults and multiply configuration, remain identical.\n\nThe core-level correctness argument follows existing ownership. Whenever in.ctrl.alu_op denotes a divide and in.valid is true, ex_stage's is_divide branch clears EX/MEM instead of capturing alu_result on every non-stalled edge. On a stalled edge EX/MEM holds and does not consume alu_result. On the completion edge the same bubble rule applies, while the sole architectural result comes from div_completion.alu_result=div_result. With invalid ID/EX entries, no retirement can observe an ordinary divide result; retain and check the existing invariant that reset/flush clear side-effect controls as well as valid. Do not rely on invalid data to suppress a side effect.\n\nKeep div_consume = is_divide && advance exactly as in the champion. Keep div_completion, retirement_w, wb_stage, normal_wb_data, register-file write-first behavior, registered binary forwarding and all pipeline control unchanged. Do not replace the dedicated div_result output with the specialized out bus. Normal-WB forwarding must still use the retained ordinary MEM/WB value; direct divide completion reaches only retirement/register-file/write-first ID as before.\n\nThis is one compile-time specialization that removes a functionally unused arithmetic-result route. It should let synthesis remove divider-result mux inputs and associated fanout from the ordinary EX result cone and avoid static paths that treat a divide as an ordinary ALU producer. It must not add result registers, alter the divider recurrence, retime completion or introduce operand masking. Preserve all branch prediction/recovery, address arithmetic, load/store handling, decoder legality, nret=1 ports and every hard invariant.\n\nThe benefit is uncertain: Gowin may already prove this route redundant through control factoring, and unchanged branch/fetch/divider paths may limit Fmax. Inspect the synthesized cone to confirm the direct divider result no longer feeds the normal EX/MEM ALU-result input, while its dedicated completion path remains. Do not count an RVFI-only pruning or circuit-neutral source change as a performance improvement. Confidence is low until all-placement vendor timing confirms a real gain.\n\nExtend ALU tests to exercise both parameter settings. With ENABLE_DIVIDE_OUT=1, retain every original output/result assertion. With it disabled, require out==0 only for the four divide opcodes while dedicated div_result, busy/done timing, reset cancellation and held completion remain bit-exact against the independent RV32M reference. Check non-divide operations remain identical in both settings. Exercise real and ALTOPS configurations without weakening either reference.\n\nIn pipeline tests, assert that an active divide never captures an ordinary EX/MEM result: memory holds preserve the prior entry, every advancing divide edge produces the existing fully inert bubble, and only direct completion retires the correct result. Cover forwarded launch operands, load-to-divide, consecutive divides, result consumers, long older memory stalls, imem stalls, reset and wrong-path divides. Retain exact RVFI operands/results/order, register consistency, trap/side-effect suppression and the unchanged ten-cycle liveness limit.\n\nRun strict lint, real/ALTOPS ALU and pipeline suites, unchanged formal and ready/stalled full-RVFI cosimulation, then canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/address/marker validation. No cycle-count change is intended: the standard stalled run should retain 4,238,604 bracketed cycles. Measure all three Gowin placement options. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s, more than 4.6 percent above 195.55, or approximately 86.699 MHz median at unchanged cycles.\n\nThis final specialization has not been prototyped or timed. Earlier independent session probes were rejected: one-hot forwarding measured 63.286 MHz median; speculative address sums 72.138 MHz; div_done-only consumption 68.326 MHz; and byte carry-select address addition 72.739 MHz. All passed ten pipeline configurations, and the two address transformations also passed arithmetic SAT checks, but none established a fitness gain. Those RTL changes have been restored and none belongs to this proposal. Their results are not validation of the final specialization.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Add a default-true ENABLE_DIVIDE_OUT parameter that controls only whether DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU select div_result onto ordinary out. When false, those arms return zero. Preserve dedicated completion, all real/ALTOPS arithmetic and every other output and handshake behavior.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Set ENABLE_DIVIDE_OUT=0 on u_alu. Preserve the original divider request/consume logic, dedicated div_result-to-div_completion connection, EX/MEM bubble discipline, forwarding and every other EX function.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Exercise both ordinary divide-output parameter settings in real and ALTOPS builds. Retain default-mode assertions and require identical dedicated results and protocol in specialized mode, with only its ordinary divide out value zero. Retain all non-divide and arithmetic correctness checks.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Strengthen direct-divider ownership checks: holds retain older EX/MEM, advancing divide edges inject inert bubbles, and only dedicated completion retires the bit-correct result. Cover dependencies, stalls, reset, wrong paths and consumers without weakening existing RVFI, side-effect or liveness assertions.'''}]\n}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef string_rep(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value or len(value)>120 else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,string_rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261003-001-r14s0' and d['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert -50 <= d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'] <= 50\nprint('Validated final hypothesis:',p)\nPY\ngit diff --exit-code\nls -l cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-001-r14s0',\n'title':'Prune the unused divide-to-EX/MEM ALU result route',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion retires DIV/REM directly from the dedicated div_result output and inserts an EX/MEM bubble on every divide edge, including consumption. However, alu.sv also selects div_result onto its ordinary combinational out bus for all four divide opcodes. That bus feeds the normal EX/MEM result cone even though no dividing instruction can capture it there. Removing this redundant result route can reduce divider-result fanout and ordinary ALU output selection without modifying arithmetic, instruction latency or any valid retirement. Recent micro_opt branch-comparator, register-file and shifter rewrites regressed; this proposal instead specializes an already separate completion interface.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Introduce a default-enabled ALU parameter named ENABLE_DIVIDE_OUT. In the ALU output case, DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU return div_result when this parameter is true and 32'b0 when false. Instantiate the EX-stage ALU with ENABLE_DIVIDE_OUT=0 alongside its existing ENABLE_MULTIPLY=0. Preserve the dedicated div_result output, divider state machine, request/busy/done/consume handshake, magnitude and sign handling, special cases and exact eight busy clocks. The parameter affects only the ordinary combinational out bus, never the actual divide completion output.\n\nThe standalone ALU defaults to the original behavior, including divide values on out for existing arithmetic tests. Apply the same output-route specialization in real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS builds, without changing any ALTOPS formula, constant or handshake. All non-divide output case arms, including defaults and multiply configuration, remain identical.\n\nThe core-level correctness argument follows existing ownership. Whenever in.ctrl.alu_op denotes a divide and in.valid is true, ex_stage's is_divide branch clears EX/MEM instead of capturing alu_result on every non-stalled edge. On a stalled edge EX/MEM holds and does not consume alu_result. On the completion edge the same bubble rule applies, while the sole architectural result comes from div_completion.alu_result=div_result. With invalid ID/EX entries, no retirement can observe an ordinary divide result; retain and check the existing invariant that reset/flush clear side-effect controls as well as valid. Do not rely on invalid data to suppress a side effect.\n\nKeep div_consume = is_divide && advance exactly as in the champion. Keep div_completion, retirement_w, wb_stage, normal_wb_data, register-file write-first behavior, registered binary forwarding and all pipeline control unchanged. Do not replace the dedicated div_result output with the specialized out bus. Normal-WB forwarding must still use the retained ordinary MEM/WB value; direct divide completion reaches only retirement/register-file/write-first ID as before.\n\nThis is one compile-time specialization that removes a functionally unused arithmetic-result route. It should let synthesis remove divider-result mux inputs and associated fanout from the ordinary EX result cone and avoid static paths that treat a divide as an ordinary ALU producer. It must not add result registers, alter the divider recurrence, retime completion or introduce operand masking. Preserve all branch prediction/recovery, address arithmetic, load/store handling, decoder legality, nret=1 ports and every hard invariant.\n\nThe benefit is uncertain: Gowin may already prove this route redundant through control factoring, and unchanged branch/fetch/divider paths may limit Fmax. Inspect the synthesized cone to confirm the direct divider result no longer feeds the normal EX/MEM ALU-result input, while its dedicated completion path remains. Do not count an RVFI-only pruning or circuit-neutral source change as a performance improvement. Confidence is low until all-placement vendor timing confirms a real gain.\n\nExtend ALU tests to exercise both parameter settings. With ENABLE_DIVIDE_OUT=1, retain every original output/result assertion. With it disabled, require out==0 only for the four divide opcodes while dedicated div_result, busy/done timing, reset cancellation and held completion remain bit-exact against the independent RV32M reference. Check non-divide operations remain identical in both settings. Exercise real and ALTOPS configurations without weakening either reference.\n\nIn pipeline tests, assert that an active divide never captures an ordinary EX/MEM result: memory holds preserve the prior entry, every advancing divide edge produces the existing fully inert bubble, and only direct completion retires the correct result. Cover forwarded launch operands, load-to-divide, consecutive divides, result consumers, long older memory stalls, imem stalls, reset and wrong-path divides. Retain exact RVFI operands/results/order, register consistency, trap/side-effect suppression and the unchanged ten-cycle liveness limit.\n\nRun strict lint, real/ALTOPS ALU and pipeline suites, unchanged formal and ready/stalled full-RVFI cosimulation, then canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/address/marker validation. No cycle-count change is intended: the standard stalled run should retain 4,238,604 bracketed cycles. Measure all three Gowin placement options. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s, more than 4.6 percent above 195.55, or approximately 86.699 MHz median at unchanged cycles.\n\nThis final specialization has not been prototyped or timed. Earlier independent session probes were rejected: one-hot forwarding measured 63.286 MHz median; speculative address sums 72.138 MHz; div_done-only consumption 68.326 MHz; and byte carry-select address addition 72.739 MHz. All passed ten pipeline configurations, and the two address transformations also passed arithmetic SAT checks, but none established a fitness gain. Those RTL changes have been restored and none belongs to this proposal. Their results are not validation of the final specialization.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Add a default-true ENABLE_DIVIDE_OUT parameter that controls only whether DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU select div_result onto ordinary out. When false, those arms return zero. Preserve dedicated completion, all real/ALTOPS arithmetic and every other output and handshake behavior.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Set ENABLE_DIVIDE_OUT=0 on u_alu. Preserve the original divider request/consume logic, dedicated div_result-to-div_completion connection, EX/MEM bubble discipline, forwarding and every other EX function.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Exercise both ordinary divide-output parameter settings in real and ALTOPS builds. Retain default-mode assertions and require identical dedicated results and protocol in specialized mode, with only its ordinary divide out value zero. Retain all non-divide and arithmetic correctness checks.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Strengthen direct-divider ownership checks: holds retain older EX/MEM, advancing divide edges inject inert bubbles, and only dedicated completion retires the bit-correct result. Cover dependencies, stalls, reset, wrong paths and consumers without weakening existing RVFI, side-effect or liveness assertions.'''}]\n}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef string_rep(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value or len(value)>120 else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,string_rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schem