ork, not division operators\nor two full-width subtractors on the operand-forwarding path.\n\nEvery busy edge, including the sixth and last, now captures step 5.\nKeep 33-bit trial remainders and 34-bit zero-extended differences with\ncorrect borrow detection. Do not shift in extra padding or discard\neffective quotient steps. Preserve signed quotient/remainder\ncorrection, divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 results. Completion and\nresult must remain stable until consumed, and reset must cancel work.\nThe real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS branches must have identic\n…[28949 of 32021 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:61b79157a2019ce3]…\non, back-to-back\noperations, both mode transitions and unchanged eight-clock completion.\nPipeline tests must cover forwarded operands, load-to-divide, consecutive\ndivides, wrong-path cancellation, older stalled memory, result consumers,\nexact RVFI operands/results/order and the unchanged ten-cycle liveness\nlimit. Run real/ALTOPS suites, unchanged formal, ready/stalled full-RVFI\ncosim, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/address/marker checks. Standard\nALTOPS formal does not prove the real recurrence; do not claim it does.\n\nPreserve nret=1, every external port, decoder legality, fetch/prediction,\nforwarding, memory semantics and all hard invariants. Measure actual\nbracketed cycles and all three Gowin options. Expected CoreMark cycles\nremain 4,238,604; at that count acceptance requires median Fmax above\n86.698653 MHz and fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s, more than\n4.6 percent over 195.55. The expected gain is a hypothesis, not a measured\nresult, and must survive the unchanged evaluation gates.\n\nnotes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
