{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_75", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r15s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261003-001-r15s0\ntitle: \\\"Align internal M-operation encoding with funct3 and execution class\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current internal ALU codes place MUL variants at 11..14 and DIV/REM\n  at 15..18, straddling binary decode boundaries. EX repeatedly compares\n  these five-bit codes to identify resource classes, including on the\n  direct-divide-retirement path to register-file writes and ID bypass.\n  Recent r14s0/r14s1 and local probes show that divider arithmetic and\n  completion/operand-control paths compete for timing. Adding separate\n  registered class flags increased decode/placement cost in a local probe.\n  Reencoding the existing five-bit field can simplify both instruction\n  decode and EX resource classification without adding any state or cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make one micro-optimization: change the internal M-extension ALU operation\n  encoding to {2'b10, instruction_funct3}. Preserve the existing RV32I codes\n  0..10. Use MUL=16, MULH=17, MULHSU=18, MULHU=19, DIV=20, DIVU=21,\n  REM=22 and REMU=23. These are internal control values, not ISA encodings;\n  instruction bits, results, legality and every externally visible behavior\n  stay identical. In particular, distinguish the funct3 ordering of MULHSU\n  and MULHU rather than blindly incrementing the old enumeration.\n\n  Multiply membership becomes alu_op[4:2]==3'b100, and divide/remainder\n  membership becomes alu_op[4:2]==3'b101. Use these exact three-bit class\n  predicates in EX and the top-level multiply/load-use classification,\n  preserving the original validity qualifications and all reset, stall,\n  launch, consume, ownership and trap terms. EX is_divide remains\n  in.valid AND the divide-class predicate. is_multiply retains its original\n  ungated classification. Do not replace these with op[4] alone: unused\n  internal codes 24..31 must not become valid resource requests.\n\n  Within the decoder's existing positively validated R-type funct7=1\n  arm, the eight operations can assign alu_op={2'b10,funct3}. Retain\n  default is_illegal=1 and clear it only within the same validated legal\n  arms as before. Leave every RV32I, SYSTEM and reserved-instruction check\n  intact. Keeping the eight symbolic case assignments is also equivalent\n  if Gowin folds them into the same wiring. Do not decode M operations\n  from funct3 without checking opcode and funct7.\n\n  Keep all arithmetic case arms symbolic. Preserve every real multiply,\n  divider recurrence, prefix, magnitude conversion, signed/unsigned choice,\n  quotient/remainder selection and exception result. Preserve the exact\n  ALTOPS formulas and constants under their corresponding symbolic op names.\n  Any simplification of signed-operation or remainder selection must match\n  the full five-bit equality predicates for all 32 possible internal codes,\n  including the now-unused code 11 and codes 12..15. No arithmetic rewrite,\n  prefix optimization, new class flop, autonomous completion, forwarding\n  encoding change or additional stage belongs to this proposal.\n\n  The intended circuit change is shallower and less duplicated operation\n  decoding: two aligned four-code groups plus direct funct3-to-low-code\n  wiring. This should shorten the existing EX opcode-to-divide-grant-to-RF\n  path and multiply eligibility paths while preserving ID/EX width and all\n  pipeline timing. It may also reduce decoder logic. Mapping and routing\n  can still dominate; confirm that vendor synthesis actually simplifies\n  these cones and judge only median fitness, not gate count or RTL brevity.\n\n  Update numeric operation references inside allowed test/test_*.py files.\n  Do not edit test/_helpers.py, which is outside the allowed test filename\n  pattern. The ALU and decoder suites can define or import their corrected\n  internal constants within allowed test files, retaining all independent\n  expected arithmetic values and ISA encodings. Update the pipeline suite's\n  MUL_OPS, synthetic divide-control constructor (old base 15 becomes 20)\n  and synthetic multiply-control constructor (old MUL 11 becomes 16).\n  Packed field widths and every assertion remain intact. Add checks for\n  unique operation codes, both exact class sets and unused-code exclusion.\n\n  Run strict lint, real/ALTOPS ALU and pipeline tests, decoder legality\n  tests, unchanged formal, and ready/stalled full-RVFI cosimulation. Keep\n  all canonical CoreMark CRCs, required UART text, bounded addresses and\n  marker-bracketed timing. The ten-cycle liveness bound, nret=1 ports,\n  retirement order, retained WB forwarding, and all hard invariants remain\n  unchanged. Expected marked CoreMark cycles are exactly 4,238,604.\n\n  The initial prefix idea was rejected after measurement: two narrow\n  radix-4 prefix steps reached 74.651 MHz median, moving only its high\n  guard reached 75.599 MHz, and a minimized Boolean prefix reached\n  75.815 MHz. Separate registered divide/multiply flags reached 72.695 MHz.\n  Those changes are excluded. A baseline rerun reproduced 82.887 MHz.\n  These are negative findings, not validation of this operation reencoding.\n  The final code assignment must be timed and validated independently.\n  Success requires median fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s,\n  more than 4.6 percent above 195.55; at unchanged cycles this requires\n  approximately 86.699 MHz. Confidence remains low until measured.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Reassign only M-extension ALU constants to 16+funct3, preserving\n      RV32I codes, the five-bit field width and every packed bundle layout.\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: |\n      Preserve validated opcode/funct legality while encoding the M arm\n      as 16+funct3 or equivalent symbolic cases. Keep all defaults and\n      reserved/SYSTEM handling unchanged.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace four-way M-class membership comparisons with exact\n      alu_op[4:2] class predicates. Preserve validity, launch, consumption,\n      forwarding-owner conditions and every existing pipeline control.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Use the aligned multiply-class predicate in the existing late-result\n      hazard expression with identical valid and memory-read qualifications.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Update local internal M-operation constants without changing the\n      protected helper file or any independent arithmetic/protocol checks.\n      Verify all operation codes and unused-code behavior in both modes.\n  - file: test/test_decoder.py\n    description: |\n      Expect the new internal operation codes for all eight ISA M encodings;\n      preserve all default-illegal, reserved encoding and SYSTEM assertions.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Update only numeric internal M-class references and synthetic control\n      constructors. Retain packed widths and all dependency, forwarding,\n      stall, divide latency, trap, RVFI and exactly-once side-effect checks.\n''')\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Refined hypothesis is schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
