{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,190p' Makefile; sed -n '1,220p' tools/eval/cosim.py; sed -n '1,130p' formal/checks_si.cfg; rg --files cores/bench/generated | head -35\"", "aggregated_output": ".PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\n# Resolve OSS CAD Suite path so commands work even when the user hasn't\n# sourced .toolchain/oss-cad-suite/environment in this shell.\nTOOLCHAIN_DIR := $(CURDIR)/.toolchain\nOSS_BIN       := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/oss-cad-suite/bin\nLOCAL_BIN     := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/bin\nexport PATH := $(OSS_BIN):$(LOCAL_BIN):$(PATH)\n\n# Orchestrator knobs (pass-through to tools.orchestrator):\n#   N        — number of rounds for `make loop` (default 10).\n#   K        — tournament size, slots per round (default 1 = sequential).\n#   AGENT    — codex (default) or claude. Honors a pre-existing\n#              AGENT_PROVIDER env var if AGENT isn't set on the make\n#              command line.\n#   BASE     — when forking a new TARGET, copy from cores/<BASE>/.\n#              Default: baseline (orchestrator-side default).\n#   COREMARK — target CoreMark iterations/sec (e.g. '370').\n#   LUT      — target LUT count (e.g. '3000').\n#   WORKTREE — default ON. `make loop` first creates a dedicated git worktree\n#              at .worktrees/<TARGET>/ on branch core-<TARGET> and re-execs\n#              itself there. Lets two `make loop` invocations for different\n#              TARGETs run in parallel without git index/merge collisions.\n#              To opt out (run directly on the current branch + cwd) pass\n#              an explicit empty value: `make loop TARGET=v1 WORKTREE=`.\nN        ?= 10\nK        ?= 1\nAGENT    ?= $(or $(AGENT_PROVIDER),codex)\nBASE     ?=\nCOREMARK ?=\nLUT      ?=\nWORKTREE ?= 1\n\n# Compose optional CLI flags for the orchestrator. Empty vars produce\n# empty strings so the orchestrator falls back to its defaults.\nORCH_FLAGS  = --iterations $(N) --tournament-size $(K)\nifneq ($(strip $(BASE)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --base $(BASE)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(COREMARK)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(LUT)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --lut-target $(LUT)\nendif\n\n# Multi-core: TARGET selects the core under cores/<TARGET>\n…[14536 of 17608 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ab8f93192488fa3a]…\n_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\nrg: cores/bench/generated: IO error for operation on cores/bench/generated: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
