wide subtract-and-select depth per four dividend bits instead of two. The cost is fifteen trial subtractors instead of six, additional constant-multiple storage, and a wider one-hot selection tree. Expect a moderate area increase within the 10,000 LUT4 target. Divisor-preparation timing, selection fanout, routing congestion, and the unchanged IF-to-ID recovery-token path can limit the benefit. This is a single divider topology proposal, not a combination with the fetch-buffer or retirement-control experiments. Those exploratory alternatives did not clear acceptance and are excluded.\n\nValidate every real M-extension operation with the unchanged exact arithmetic tests and additional independent randomized quotient/remainder checks, particularly large unsigned divisors, signed extremes and trial values around each digit boundary k*D. Exercise divisor values whose multiples need all 36 bits. Check the recurrence invariant and one-hot digit selection for nonzero divisors against an independent arithmetic reference. Preserve ALTOPS testing, all standard formal checks including the ten-cycle retirement liveness bound, and full-RVFI ready/stalled cosimulation. Keep canonical CoreMark CRCs, UART validation, address bounds and marker-bracketed timing unchanged. Real arithmetic must be checked independently because standard formal uses ALTOPS; do not claim that gate proves the new recurrence.\n\nMeasure all three vendor placement options and actual marked CoreMark cycles. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s, more than 4.6 percent above 195.55. If the expected 4,238,604-cycle interval is retained, median Fmax must exceed 86.698653 MHz. The expected gain below is a hypothesis, not a measured claim; final implementation must satisfy the unchanged gates.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':9,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Replace only the real divider's two-stage radix-4 recurrence with fifteen par