{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r11s1.yaml'); d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Radix-16 divider with an independent completion grant'\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('Make one structural change to the shared real DIV/REM datapath:', 'Restructure the shared DIV/REM resource around a shorter recurrence and its own registered completion token:')\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('Retain the launch-time unsigned magnitude conversion,', '''Complete the same resource restructuring at its retirement interface. In ex_stage.sv drive div_consume = div_done AND NOT normal_wb_valid AND NOT stall AND NOT reset, and continue driving div_completion.valid from div_consume. Remove the redundant live EX is_divide/advance qualification from this grant. Keep execute_wait and advance otherwise unchanged. The divider's registered done bit already proves ownership: requests require a valid decoded divide; ID/EX is held until completion; older branches have resolved before launch; and no younger instruction can replace this owner before consumption. Thus done implies the matching valid divide still owns ID/EX. Preserve the existing older-WB arbitration, dmem backpressure, reset cancellation and retained-completion tests. Do not remove these protections or change the externally observable request/consume protocol. This avoids letting live EX opcode decode feed the direct-retirement selection and register-file write path after the recurrence is shortened.\n\nRetain the launch-time unsigned magnitude conversion,''')\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('architectural completion ownership, memory interfaces', 'in-order architectural retirement ownership, memory interfaces')\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('This is a single divider topology proposal,