{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nwanted={'hyp-20261002-003-r8s2','hyp-20261003-002-r10s1','hyp-20261003-003-r10s2','hyp-20261003-001-r10s0'}\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('id') in wanted:\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes'))\n  print('PATH',d.get('critical_path'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-003-r8s2 Two-entry predictor run-ahead on the fabric-register-file core\nAdd a two-entry fixed-head elastic queue to the existing predicted\ninstruction stream on the supplied champion. The single change is\nprediction-driven fetch run-ahead across load-use, memory and execute\nholds. Retain the 128-entry bimodal table, direct-JAL prediction,\nsequential JALR policy, frozen direction-token recovery, pipeline\nboundaries, fabric register file, registered forwarding and divider.\n\nEach entry stores instruction[31:0], PC[19:2] and predicted_direct,\ntotaling 51 bits. Store only aligned PCs in [0,0x00100000). Reconstruct\nfull saved PCs by zero extension; retain full-width live PC, target\narithmetic, recovery and architectural address semantics. Entry zero\nalways supplies the oldest buffered instruction. Empty bypass preserves\nthe existing no-extra-stage behavior. Head selection depends only on\noccupancy and raw bus availability, never on decode acceptance.\n\nGive IF independent raw bus_ready and decode_hold inputs. Existing\nstall_id supplies decode_hold. Return available = nonempty OR bus_ready\nto hazard control in place of raw imemReady. Define consume = available\nAND NOT decode_hold, pop = nonempty AND consume, and accept = bus_ready\nAND (count < 2 OR pop), subject to the boundary restriction below.\nAppend an accepted response exactly when nonempty OR NOT consume; an\nempty response consumed directly is never also enqueued. Every accepted\nresponse advances the fetch PC using its own prediction even while\ndecode is held. Otherwise retain the fetch PC.\n\nOn pop, shift remaining occupied entries toward the fixed head. Append\nat old count minus pop with priority over a shift to the same entry.\nUse an explicitly sized two-bit occupancy count and constant-index\npayload banks with local enables; avoid variable-index head reads.\nSimultaneous full pop/push keeps occupancy two and replaces the tail.\nClear occupancy on reset/recovery; unused payload need not be reset.\nCompute candidate payload writes without redirect in the\n…[26606 of 29678 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:90970eb7f5147f3d]…\n 177.89 by\n**9.92894%**. At this cycle count the required median is 78.868951 MHz.\n\nOption-zero resources: **5,048 logic cells, 1,832 registers, 0 LUT-RAM, 4 BSRAM,\n6 DSP**. Its worst reported setup path starts at the benchmark instruction LFSR\nand ends at ID/EX `recovery_static_miss`, through IF and ID.\n\n## Remaining considerations\n\nJALR target arithmetic still drives the fetch-PC data input. The deliberate\nrecovery bubble for a sequential or trapping JALR can cost cycles on instruction\nstreams other than this CoreMark workload. Placement results are sensitive to\nequivalent combinational factoring; the numbers above are measurements of the\nfinal RTL, not the supplied prototype's results.\n\nFinal RTL fingerprint (`sha256sum cores/bench/rtl/*.sv | sha256sum`):\n`f12aac79ecd272c2c4d79f76861efe153b88470eea91f3dfda2b9d5c19ae9f43`.\n\nPATH {'from': 'lfsr_3_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.recovery_static_miss_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.85, 'arrival_ns': 18.144, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The prior fetch queues reduced CoreMark cycles by about 5%, but their empty-queue bypass retained the long fetch-to-decode path. I’m focusing on a registered fetch/decode boundary with two buffer entries: it could cut that path and hide bus stalls, at the cost of one extra cycle on recovery."}}
