{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_46", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r12s1.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261003-002-r12s1\ntitle: \\\"Resolve branch comparisons before forwarding selection\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 195.55 iterations/s at 82.887 MHz with 4,238,604\n  marked CoreMark cycles. Registered forwarding selectors improved the\n  operand path in r7s0, but branch recovery still serializes a wide operand\n  forwarding mux, a 32-bit comparison and recovery selection. Recent paths\n  repeatedly start at forwarding-selector flops and end at the fetch PC.\n  Structural r10s1 moved recovery to a later stage at a cycle cost; r10s2\n  instead predecoded recovery tokens. The remaining opportunity is to\n  change the branch unit's relationship to operand forwarding. The failed\n  r10s0 nibble comparator cautions against rebuilding the comparator itself.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make one structural change to the execute branch unit: duplicate branch\n  comparisons across candidate forwarding sources and select the resulting\n  one-bit predicates after comparison. Keep ordinary ALU, address, store\n  and RVFI operand forwarding unchanged. This moves branch bypass\n  selection to the result side of the comparators without adding a stage,\n  changing prediction policy, or spending an extra recovery cycle.\n\n  Define rs1 candidates A[0]=in.rs1_val, A[1]=fwd_ex_mem,\n  A[2]=fwd_mem_wb, and rs2 candidates B[0]=in.rs2_val,\n  B[1]=fwd_ex_mem, B[2]=fwd_mem_wb. These are registered data sources,\n  including retained ordinary WB during a memory stall. For each of the\n  nine constant-index pairs compute equality and an ordered comparison\n  concurrently, before selecting which forwarding sources own rs1/rs2.\n  Normalize signed order exactly as the champion does: XOR each operand's\n  sign bit with NOT branch_op[1], then use full-width unsigned less-than.\n  Preserve ordinary equality on the unmodified bits. Pairs selecting the\n  same shared forwarding word have equality one and less-than zero and\n  should collapse to constants. Let synthesis share common logic; do not\n  create a manual nibble comparator or a priority comparison chain.\n\n  Decode existing registered fwd_rs1_sel and fwd_rs2_sel independently to\n  three one-hot source enables. Encoding 1 selects EX/MEM, 2 selects\n  retained MEM/WB, and both 0 and existing default encoding 3 select the\n  corresponding ID/EX operand. Pair (i,j) selection is the AND of those\n  two enables. Reduce masked equality bits with an OR; independently\n  reduce masked less-than bits. Use the original branch-op case to select\n  equality for BEQ/BNE and ordered comparison for the four ordering\n  branches. Preserve branch_base=0 for reserved funct3, branch polarity\n  XOR and the reserved branch_cond=0 rule. Recovery still uses current\n  predecoded tokens and selected branch_base. Candidate comparators must\n  not consume rs1/rs2 after the ordinary forwarding mux, which would\n  restore the serial path.\n\n  Preserve forwarding-selector capture/hold/squash, youngest-writer and\n  x0 rules, load/multiply interlocks and speculative JALR ownership.\n  Keep exact advance gating, dmem hold priority, BHT training, direct\n  offset-four behavior, alignment traps, unconditional legal-JALR recovery,\n  full-width target adders and actual_next_pc. Normal forwarded rs1/rs2\n  remain the architectural operand values recorded in RVFI. Only the\n  selected candidate predicate may affect architectural execution. Keep\n  the register file, arithmetic resources, fetch/decode topology, all\n  instruction latencies, retirement boundary, nret=1 and ports unchanged.\n\n  Bypass-selector paths now traverse a small predicate mux instead of\n  a wide operand mux followed by comparison. Source-data paths still\n  traverse a comparator and predicate selection. Replication costs LUTs\n  and routing; the divider, JALR target or IF-to-ID path may limit Fmax.\n  This is one branch-unit area-for-delay hypothesis.\n\n  Validate equivalence to the original forwarded-operand branch function\n  for arbitrary four 32-bit source words, every forwarding-select encoding\n  and all eight funct3 values. Include equal shared sources, opposite\n  signs, signed extrema, different forwarding sources, retained WB during\n  long dmem stalls and back-to-back writers. Preserve existing prediction-\n  token equivalence, decoder, trap, wrong-path side-effect and RVFI checks.\n  Run real/ALTOPS pipeline tests, unchanged formal including ten-cycle\n  liveness, full-RVFI ready/stalled cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/\n  address/marker checks. Expect the same 4,238,604 marked CoreMark cycles.\n  Measure all three Gowin placement options. At unchanged cycles,\n  acceptance requires median Fmax above 86.698653 MHz and fitness above\n  204.5453 iterations/s, more than 4.6 percent above the champion.\n\n  Exploratory exclusions: a mandatory registered two-entry fetch buffer\n  passed all 53 formal checks and reduced CoreMark to 4,089,805 cycles,\n  but its 73.276 MHz median erased the gain. A radix-16 divider with a\n  parallel prefix passed real/ALTOPS arithmetic and cosim but reached\n  only 76.8 MHz median. Neither change belongs to this proposal. These\n  results reinforce targeting the remaining forwarding/recovery structure.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the single post-forwarding branch comparator with full-width\n      equality/ordered candidate comparisons and one-hot masked predicate\n      selection using existing registered forwarding owners. Preserve all\n      other operand forwarding, branch recovery, training, traps, targets,\n      arithmetic, hold and retirement logic and latencies.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add independent equivalence coverage of candidate-predicate selection\n      versus the original branch function for every source-select/funct3\n      combination and directed shared-source/signed-boundary cases. Exercise\n      both bypass stages and retained WB under stalls. Keep every existing\n      architectural, recovery, side-effect and liveness assertion intact.\nYAML\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r12s1.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()));print('Schema validation passed')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
