{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"agent_message","text":"The recovery variants all regressed, so I’m replacing that proposal. The final hypothesis will target the divider with one width-based schedule: divisors ≥256 need at most 24 quotient bits, allowing eight radix-8 steps; smaller divisors can use a narrow datapath for eight radix-16 steps. This preserves the retirement bound while removing the two wide subtract/select stages from each iteration. I’ll check the arithmetic model before finalizing the YAML."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport random\nM=(1<<32)-1\nrng=random.Random(0x131)\ndef trial_step(r,q,d,bits):\n t=(r<<bits)|(q>>(32-bits))\n ge=[t>=k*d for k in range(1,1<<bits)]\n weights=[not ge[0]]+[ge[k-1] and not ge[k] for k in range(1,(1<<bits)-1)]+[ge[-1]]\n assert sum(weights)==1\n digit=next(k for k,w in enumerate(weights) if w)\n nr=t-digit*d\n return nr,((q<<bits)|digit)&M\n\ndef model(a,d):\n large=d>=256\n q=((a&0xffffff)<<8) if large else a\n r=(a>>24) if large else 0\n for i in range(8):\n  if large:\n   assert 7*d < (1<<35)\n   if i==0:\n    prefix=(r<<3)|(q>>29)\n    assert prefix < 2048\n    if d>=2048:\n     r,q=prefix,(q<<3)&M\n    else:\n     assert 7*d<(1<<14)\n     r,q=trial_step(r,q,d,3)\n   else:\n    r,q=trial_step(r,q,d,3)\n  else:\n   for _ in range(2):\n    r,q=trial_step(r,q,d,2)\n    r&=255\n  if d: assert r<d\n return (q,r) if d else (M,a)\nvalues=[0,1,2,3,15,16,127,128,254,255,256,257,1023,1024,2047,2048,65535,65536,0x7fffffff,0x80000000,0xfffffffe,M]\npairs=[(a,d) for a in values for d in values]\npairs += [(rng.getrandbits(32),d) for d in range(513) for _ in range(30)]\npairs += [(rng.getrandbits(32),rng.getrandbits(32)) for _ in range(60000)]\nfor a,d in pairs:\n q,r=model(a,d)\n assert (q,r)==((a//d,a%d) if d else (M,a)),(a,d,q,r)\nfor _ in range(20000):\n a=rng.randrange(-(1<<31),1<<31)\n b=rng.choice(values+[-x for x in values])\n b=((b+(1<<31))&M)-(1<<31)\n q,r=model(abs(a),abs(b))\n if b:\n  q=(-q if (a<0)\"'!=(b<0) else q)&M\n  r=(-r if a<0 else r)&M\n  expected_q=(abs(a)//abs(b))*(-1 if (a<0)!=(b<0) else 1)\n  assert (q,r)==(expected_q&M,(a-expected_q*b)&M)\n else:\n  assert q==M and r==(abs(a)&M)\nprint('\"'PASS:',len(pairs),'unsigned quotient/remainder pairs; 20000 signed pairs; eight iterations and width bounds checked')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
