{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261002-001-r8s0','hyp-20261002-001-r9s0']:\n  print(d['id'],d['title'],d['outcome'],d['fmax_mhz'],d['critical_path'])\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-001-r8s0 Reduce dependent selection in M-extension arithmetic regression 67.545 {'from': 'cpu/u_fwd/fwd_rs1_1_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_12_s0', 'slack_ns': -9.586, 'arrival_ns': 19.88, 'logic_cells': 12, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nReduce dependent arithmetic and result-selection depth inside alu.sv:\nuse two parallel-trial radix-4 digits in the divider and one multiplier\nwhose signed operand extensions select the M operation before the\nproduct. This is a single micro_opt proposal for M-extension mapping,\nwith no pipeline, predictor or memory redesign. Replace the real\ndivider's four serial binary restoring steps per busy clock with two\nradix-4 restoring digit steps. Retain exactly\neight busy iteration clocks, the existing launch/done/consume protocol,\ndirect divide retirement, and nret=1. Process four dividend bits per\niteration as before; add no preparation, correction or pipeline cycle.\n\nAt the existing launch edge capture unsigned divisor magnitude D and\nits 34-bit multiple 3D. Compute 3D from the current launch operand's\nmagnitude, never the previous divisor_q. Explicitly zero-extend before\nshifting and adding so that 3*0xffffffff is represented exactly.\nDerive 34-bit D and 2D by wiring from divisor_q. Hold the registered\nmultiples throughout busy and done; reset the new register normally.\nThis removes divisor-multiple generation from the recurrent path.\n\nEach digit step takes 32-bit remainder R and quotient Q, forms the\n34-bit trial T={R,Q[31:30]}, and computes three independent 35-bit\nunsigned differences diff[k]={1'b0,T}-{1'b0,M[k]}, with 34-bit\nM[1]=D, M[2]=2D and M[3]=3D. Set ge[k]=!diff[k][34]. These widths\nare required for full-range unsigned division; do not truncate high\ndivisor bits or use prefix-width tapering in a reused iterative step.\n\nUse mutually exclusive selects s0=!ge[1], s1=ge[1]&&!ge[2],\ns2=ge[2]&&!ge[3], s3=ge[3]. Select the next 32-bit remainder with\na balanced OR of four masked candidates: T[31:0], diff[1][31:0],\ndiff[2]\n…[8685 of 11757 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d7aee05164ef9228]…\ny above 176.88906 iter/s, more than 4.6 percent above 169.11,\ncorresponding to approximately 74.334 MHz at the unchanged cycle count.\nDo not change evaluator, benchmark, formal or interface contracts.\n\nPreliminary exploration is negative evidence about nearby alternatives,\nnot a measured claim for this final circuit: preselected WB with flat\nEX operand masks and the original multipliers reached 70.146 MHz.\nAdding the shared multiplier to that flat-mux variant reached 73.606\nMHz, about 3.6 percent above the champion and below acceptance. It used\n5,043 logic cells, 1,825 registers, zero LUT-RAM, four BSRAMs and two\nDSPs; all 53 standard formal checks, 13 ALU/pipeline configurations,\nselftest and canonical CoreMark passed. Registering divide ownership\nin that variant made timing worse and is excluded. The proposed final\ncircuit retains the original EX operand muxes and opcode decoding to\navoid those additional routing changes. Final measurements must be\nreproduced by the implementation phase before acceptance.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
