{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nwanted={'hyp-20261002-002-r7s1','hyp-20261003-002-r12s1','hyp-20261003-002-r10s1'}\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in wanted:\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  print(h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-002-r7s1 Register operand delivery before EX forwarding and recovery\nMake one structural change: move register selection and source/destination\nmatching ahead of a physical operand-delivery boundary. Use 31 explicit,\nindependently written 32-bit RF flop banks with decoded one-hot reads, and\nregister forwarding-match tokens alongside the existing ID/EX operands. The existing\nID/EX operand registers must remain a real physical pipeline boundary,\nseparating register selection from EX forwarding, arithmetic and recovery.\nKeep the architectural reg_file interface and all pipeline cycle\nboundaries unchanged; this is a storage and operand-collection topology\nchange, not an added pipeline stage or an ISA change.\n\nGive each x1..x31 bank a statically elaborated data register and a local\nwrite enable w_en && w_addr == bank_number. Reset each bank to zero as\nbefore. Do not code the bank writes as a variable-index memory access, and\ndo not code reads as regs[rs_addr]; these encourage the same inferred BSRAM\nand output-register absorption as the champion. Decode each read address\nonce into 31 one-hot selects, mask each bank's word, and OR the selected\nwords with an explicitly balanced tree if needed to keep synthesis from\nbuilding a serial priority chain. x0 is a constant zero and has no writable\nbank. Preserve the exact same-cycle write-first read bypass, including\npriority of x0 over bypass and independent matching for rs1 and rs2.\n\nUse portable synthesizable SystemVerilog and structurally elaborated fixed\nbank accesses. No vendor black boxes or simulation-only implementation may\nreplace the functional register file. Verify in Gowin's synthesis report\nthat the RF is implemented as flop banks and that ID/EX operand values have\nphysical flop endpoints rather than only registered RAM addresses and\npost-RAM bypass logic. The expected cost is about 992 storage flops plus\nread selection logic, offset by removing the two RF BSRAMs. Keep within the\nTang Nano 20K's resources and the 10,000-LUT target. All 32 architectura\n…[23597 of 26669 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:37b86cfc87ae1303]…\nsult/trap/order and exactly-once\nrecovery. Adapt stage-specific timing tests while retaining every\narchitectural assertion. Run real/ALTOPS pipeline tests, unchanged formal,\nfull-RVFI ready/stalled cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker\nvalidation. Measure actual marked cycles and all three Gowin options.\nAcceptance requires fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s.\n\nPrior and exploratory evidence does not establish a measured win for\nthis final structure. In this slot, a registered fetch buffer reduced\ncycles but reached only 73.276 MHz median; a parallel-prefix radix-16\ndivider reached 76.8 MHz; replicated pre-forwarding branch comparisons\nreached 68.316 MHz. Retiming every recovery on the current champion\npassed all 53 formal checks but reached 75.086 MHz and 4,306,908 cycles.\nThose changes are excluded. The final hypothesis narrows retiming to\nJALR, retains immediate direct recovery/training, and gives indirect\ntargets dedicated storage rather than reusing shared EX/MEM pc_next.\n\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
