nd canonical CoreMark at the unchanged 4,238,604 cycles,\n  but reached only 77.630 MHz median. It is excluded from this proposal.\n  A related squash-separated operand probe also supplies no evidence\n  of acceptance. Restore all exploratory RTL before handing off this\n  hypothesis. Measure actual marked cycles and the median of all three\n  Gowin placement options for the final architecture. Acceptance needs\n  fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s; resource savings or\n  fewer dependency bubbles alone do not establish a win.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Extend EX/MEM with two registered late-source selectors, branch\n      prediction/recovery tokens and jump recovery ownership. Carry\n      registered branch target and fall-through data through the real\n      completion boundary without altering architectural port types.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Route valid, trap-qualified next-WB ownership to EX's branch\n      source-match capture. Connect MEM recovery and training to fetch\n      and hazards and send the older recovery to EX for squash priority.\n      Classify validated incoming conditional branches for the selective\n      late-result hazard exemption; preserve nret=1 and retirement muxes.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Exempt only validated conditional branches from load/multiply-use\n      interlocks because they consume operands one stage later. Preserve\n      all other hazards, dmem/divide holds, imem semantics and recovery\n      priority, using MEM's accepted recovery event.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Collect branch source values, register actual next-WB source\n      matches, targets and prediction tokens, and defer comparison and\n      branch alignment traps to MEM. Register JAL/JALR recovery events.\n      On older MEM recovery suppress younger execution/divide launch\n      and inject an inert EX/MEM bubble while permitting older retirement.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Resolve conditional operands with the registered normal-WB late\n      bypass, perform branch comparison, traps and recovery here, and\n      retire corrected source values and next PC. Emit accepted jump\n      recovery and exactly-once branch training from the same boundary.\n      Retain load/multiply completion, memory handshakes and WB holding.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check late load/multiply-to-branch operands, trap-cancelled writers,\n      branch/jump recovery precedence and wrong-path cancellation with\n      adversarial bus holds. Update internal stage-timing expectations\n      while preserving exact RVFI, arithmetic, memory effects, legality\n      and the unchanged ten-cycle liveness assertions.\n''')\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261003-002-r15s1' and d['category']=='structural'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Revised structural hypothesis written and schema validated.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Revised structural hypothesis written and schema validated.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
