{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print(d['id'], d['title'], d.get('outcome'), 'fitness',d.get('fitness'),'cycles',d.get('cycles'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict):\n   print(h.get('motivation',''))\n   if any(t in d['id'] for t in ['r4s2','r6s2','r7s2']):print(h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  n=d.get('implementation_notes','')\n  if n:print(n)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-003-r1s2 Early direct-control-flow prediction with a small bimodal table improvement fitness 13.38 cycles 4202272\nThe baseline predicts every control transfer sequentially and flushes on every\ntaken conditional branch, JAL, or JALR. Its IF/ID bundle is combinational, so a\ntaken transfer normally wastes one issue opportunity, not two. CoreMark's\nrepeated loops and direct calls should make many of these bubbles avoidable.\nThe only recorded experiment is the baseline; LESSONS.md is absent and there\nare no previous predictor results. The measured critical path is through\nforwarding and the combinational ALU, so this proposal targets iterations per\ncycle while keeping added prediction logic out of that arithmetic path.\n\nhyp-20261002-003-r2s2 Prediction-driven fetch ahead across execute backpressure regression fitness 13.99 cycles 3980323\nThe previous predictor hypothesis improved fitness to 13.38 by adding a\n128-entry bimodal table and early direct-JAL targets. Its measured critical\npath still runs through the execute ALU. A fresh trace of the unchanged\nchampion reproduces 4,202,272 bracketed CoreMark cycles and contains\n2,922,016 instructions, 529,588 conditional branches and only 13,735 JALRs.\nAn architectural branch-trace replay estimates 54,467 direction misses\nfor the existing bimodal table; a larger table saves only about 15,000.\nThese are replay estimates, not exact pipeline misprediction counters.\nBetter direction or return prediction alone has insufficient cycle-saving\nheadroom for the required 4.6 percent gain. The valuable unused capability\nof the existing predictor is producing a speculative fetch stream while\ndecode is blocked: today stall_if freezes the fetch PC on load-use and\ndata-memory stalls even when the instruction bus could deliver data.\n\nhyp-20261002-003-r3s2 Compact prediction-token fetch ahead on the iterative-divider core regression fitness 78.61 cycles 3980323\nThe champion already predicts direct JAL and conditional branches with a\n128-entry bimodal table. Prior branch-trace ana\n…[20062 of 23134 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:caa5084a87c43ac6]…\ndirection or return prediction alone has insufficient headroom.\n\nhyp-20261002-003-r9s2 Pipeline branch-predictor training to isolate execute fanout regression fitness 160.6 cycles 4202272\nDirect prediction already removes most branch bubbles. Earlier trace\nreplay found only 54,467 conditional misses in 4,202,272 CoreMark cycles,\nmaking accuracy alone unlikely to clear the 4.6 percent threshold.\nFresh experiments on this champion also reject another stream queue:\ntwo entries reached 3,991,298 cycles but only 66.228 MHz median; three\nentries with registered-capacity admission reached 3,988,312 cycles but\nonly 67.208 MHz. Their saved cycles did not compensate for timing cost.\nSeveral near-critical paths run from forwarded EX operands through\nbranch resolution into the BHT counter registers. The current branch\nresult and advancing enable directly drive 128 local counter updates.\nIsolating that training fanout is a smaller, previously untried predictor\nchange that leaves the instruction delivery datapath intact.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
