{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261003-003-r10s2','hyp-20261003-003-r11s2']:\n  print(d['id'])\n  print('critical_path',d.get('critical_path'))\n  print('seeds',d.get('seeds'))\n  print('notes',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\ncommand -v gw_sh; command -v verilator; command -v pytest; rg --files --hidden -g '*.elf' -g '*.fs' -g '*timing*' -g 'gw_sh' | head -30\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-003-r10s2\ncritical_path {'from': 'lfsr_3_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.recovery_static_miss_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.85, 'arrival_ns': 18.144, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id']}\nseeds [77.823, 82.887, 82.887]\nnotes # Predictor recovery tokens\n\nImplemented the complete recovery-token protocol in `cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv`,\n`id_stage.sv`, and `ex_stage.sv`. Extended only `cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- ID/EX now freezes `branch_prediction_xor`, `recovery_branch_check`, and\n  `recovery_static_miss` with the accepted instruction. Direct alignment uses a\n  two-bit PC-plus-immediate sum, explicitly truncated modulo four. Existing\n  reset/squash/hold priority applies to the complete bundle. Original prediction\n  metadata is retained for independent checks.\n- EX shares one equality comparison and one unsigned ordered comparison, with\n  both operand sign bits biased for signed branches. Branch polarity is applied\n  with XOR; reserved branch funct3 values retain the false architectural outcome.\n  Direct recovery uses only the registered tokens and the base comparison.\n- Every advancing valid legal JALR recovers, including sequential and misaligned\n  targets. Full-width target arithmetic, bit-zero clearing, trap fall-through,\n  architectural link-write suppression, and RVFI remain unchanged.\n- The specul