{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261002-003-r9s2','hyp-20261003-003-r11s2','hyp-20261003-003-r12s2']:\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'], '\\\\n',h.get('motivation',''), '\\\\n',h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261002-003-r9s2 \n Direct prediction already removes most branch bubbles. Earlier trace\nreplay found only 54,467 conditional misses in 4,202,272 CoreMark cycles,\nmaking accuracy alone unlikely to clear the 4.6 percent threshold.\nFresh experiments on this champion also reject another stream queue:\ntwo entries reached 3,991,298 cycles but only 66.228 MHz median; three\nentries with registered-capacity admission reached 3,988,312 cycles but\nonly 67.208 MHz. Their saved cycles did not compensate for timing cost.\nSeveral near-critical paths run from forwarded EX operands through\nbranch resolution into the BHT counter registers. The current branch\nresult and advancing enable directly drive 128 local counter updates.\nIsolating that training fanout is a smaller, previously untried predictor\nchange that leaves the instruction delivery datapath intact.\n \n Add one clock of pipelining to BHT training inside if_stage. Register a\nnine-bit event consisting of valid, branch_pc[8:2], and branch_taken.\nEach clock capture valid = branch_update, including zero on cycles\nwithout an advancing legal branch. Capture index and outcome only when\nbranch_update is asserted. Reset clears the pending event. Keep the\nexisting EX generation of branch_update: only a valid, legal, nontrapping\nconditional branch that advances can emit an event. Do not change EX\nrecovery, branch comparisons, operand forwarding or pipeline holds.\n\n