{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r14s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-003-r14s2',\n'title':'Banked write-behind BHT with coherent prediction forwarding',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 195.55 iterations/s at 82.887 MHz with 4,238,604 marked CoreMark cycles. Prior replay found too few direction misses for accuracy alone to clear the 4.6 percent acceptance margin. Several recent vendor paths run from forwarded EX branch operands into BHT counters. Direct EX training currently drives 128 address-qualified saturating state machines. Earlier delayed training regressed on the old multiplier topology; a fresh scalar-event probe on this champion also reached only 78.206 MHz. The proposed architectural change is a banked, predecoded write-behind direction predictor whose pending update is forwarded to prediction reads, preserving the champion's complete prediction sequence while isolating late branch resolution from counter-array update logic.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the physical organization and training interface inside the existing 128-entry, two-bit bimodal BHT with eight banks of sixteen counters and a one-entry registered training stage. This is one predictor architecture change. Retain the exact PC[8:2] index, four-state saturating policy, weakly-not-taken initialization, raw-instruction predecode, direct-target arithmetic and alignment/range guards. Do not add a target cache, history predictor, fetch queue, pipeline bubble, or architectural recovery stage.\n\nSplit the resolving index into bank = branch_pc[8:6] and row = branch_pc[5:2]. Register an eight-bit one-hot bank select and a sixteen-bit one-hot row select, along with valid and outcome: 26 event flops total. Capture both decodes and branch_taken unconditionally each clock, independently of branch_update, front-end acceptance and EX holds. Only valid is assigned branch_update and cleared on reset. The existing branch_update already qualifies exactly one advancing legal nontrapping conditional branch; preserve its exact qualification, including allowing an untaken branch whose hypothetical target is misaligned. Never add a combinational pending-event or EX-result bypass around this register boundary.\n\nOn every clock, each constant-index local counter consumes the PREVIOUS event iff pending_valid AND pending_bank[bank] AND pending_row[row]. Apply the same local two-bit saturating increment/decrement as the champion. Independently capture the next event on that edge. Thus one branch per cycle is supported without an event FIFO or backpressure. Drain a pending event even when instruction fetch or EX is held or a later instruction recovers: it belongs to an already advancing branch. Reset alone discards the pending event and initializes all counters to 01. Invalid event payload is irrelevant and must be masked before it can affect prediction or state. Do not hold or conditionally enable payload capture using the late branch-update signal; that signal should drive only the event-valid flop, not the counter array or event-address payload enables.\n\nOrganize fetch reads as a shallow, explicit two-level bank read. Decode fetch PC[5:2] once into sixteen row selects. Within each of eight banks, OR-reduce sixteen constant-index masked two-bit counter leaves using a balanced tree. Select the bank using PC[8:6], preferably a balanced masked-OR bank selection. Use fabric counters and local synchronous updates, not a RAM read-modify-write port. Keep row and bank address decoding separate rather than reconstructing a seven-bit dynamic array index or a flat 128-way tag comparison. The implementation should expose these groups structurally; ordinary synthesis remains authoritative, with no contract or timing constraints changed.\n\nMake lookup coherent with immediate-resolution training using only registered pending state. Let C be the stored two-bit counter selected by the current fetch PC. A pending hit is pending_valid AND pending_bank[PC[8:6]] AND pending_row[PC[5:2]]. The direction after saturating one pending outcome differs from C[1] only when C is weak (01 or 10). Therefore effective_taken = pending_hit AND (C[1] XOR C[0]) ? pending_taken : C[1]. Use effective_taken exactly where the champion uses the BHT MSB. This forwarding adds no dependency on the currently resolving branch's combinational outcome. Preserve the complete two-bit counter in storage; forward only its prediction bit, without a second saturating-update datapath in fetch.\n\nThe state invariant is that applying the single valid pending event to the stored array yields the reference BHT trained at the champion's original resolution edge. Before each edge, both PC advancement and accepted ID/EX metadata use the same effective pre-edge prediction. At the edge, the old event updates storage while the next event replaces it. Consecutive branches to the same index, opposite outcomes, saturation and same-cycle lookup/update consequently reproduce the reference exactly; no training event is dropped or applied twice. This is stronger than accepting a one-event-stale table, and it requires the read forwarding even though the measured CoreMark trace happened to be insensitive to one clock of stale training in the simpler probe.\n\nLeave IF prediction consumption, all reset/recovery/hold priorities, frozen prediction metadata, decode recovery tokens, direct offset-four handling, unconditional legal JALR recovery, forwarding ownership, divider, memory completion, nret=1 and external IO unchanged. No new controls need cross core.sv: use the existing branch-update inputs of if_stage. Architectural actual_next_pc and RVFI remain authoritative; speculative addresses retain the existing full-width guarded policy. No test or correctness gate may be weakened.\n\nThe intended timing gain comes from terminating late EX training at a small event register, moving bank/row decoding before that boundary, and localizing counter/read selection. The coherent read path preserves the original prediction sequence and should preserve all 4,238,604 measured cycles, so acceptance needs median Gowin Fmax above 86.698653 MHz, yielding fitness strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s. Expected gain is seven percent with low confidence: registered-update experiments have exposed other limiting paths, and the extra counter-bit read plus forwarding mux may offset the bank organization's benefit.\n\nThis exact banked, split-decoded design has not been implemented or timed. A 200,000-cycle independent software model verified coherent write-behind lookup against an immediate-training reference, including resets, pending-row hits, repeated same-row events and opposite outcomes. That is an algorithm check, not RTL or timing validation. Fresh alternatives excluded from this proposal passed selftest/CoreMark cosimulation but regressed in median Fmax: producer-generated recovery certificates 69.697 MHz, scalar delayed training without forwarding 78.206 MHz, registered opposite-path correction addresses 71.841 MHz, and a one-bit last-outcome table 74.603 MHz. Those results justify low confidence and must not be described as evidence of a measured improvement for this final architecture.\n\nValidate an independent cycle-level reference BHT at every accepted fetch, rather than only comparing final CoreMark CRCs. Check all 128 entries, one-hot bank/row capture, reset with a pending event, back-to-back same and different rows/banks, aliasing PCs, saturation, simultaneous lookup/training, idle cycles and changing raw inputs during holds. Check stored-plus-pending equivalence to the original counter state and identical fetch PCs, predictions, recovery pulses and architectural retirements under deterministic ready patterns. Retain all existing pipeline assertions, especially exactly-once branch_update, stable held prediction tokens, reserved encodings, misaligned targets and no wrong-path memory or divide effects. Run unchanged single-channel formal including ten-cycle liveness, real/ALTOPS unit tests, full-RVFI ready/stalled cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/markers. Measure all three Gowin placement options and actual marked cycles; no unmeasured fitness gain is claimed.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Reorganize the existing bimodal BHT as eight fabric banks of sixteen counters. Add the 26-bit valid/outcome/one-hot-bank/one-hot-row training stage with unconditional payload capture, local delayed saturating updates, hierarchical masked reads, and coherent pending-event direction forwarding. Preserve existing fetch policy, all module ports, acceptance and recovery priorities.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Add an independent immediate-training BHT reference and verify lookup equivalence to the banked stored-plus-pending state, including every bank/row, pending hit/miss, consecutive aliased outcomes, saturation, reset and holds. Adapt internal storage observations to the banked representation while retaining every architectural and exactly-once training assertion. Check identical accepted PC/prediction/recovery traces, real/ALTOPS behavior, bus-stalled wrong-path suppression, and unchanged marked CoreMark cycles.'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=95,default_flow_style=False))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Replaced rejected provisional candidate with schema-valid banked coherent-training hypothesis.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
