{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261003-003-r12s2','hyp-20261003-003-r13s2','hyp-20261003-003-r11s2']:\n  print(d['id'])\n  print(d['hypothesis']['motivation'])\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\nrg -n 'timing:|cosim:|fpga:|NRET|all-options' Makefile test/cosim/build.sh tools/eval/gowin.py\nls /srv/hwebench/tmp/92f133a1/b48e2335\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-003-r11s2\nThe champion reaches 195.55 iterations/second at 82.887 MHz with\n4,238,604 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its latest reported worst\npath starts at the instruction source and passes through IF into\nID/EX recovery_static_miss. The predictor currently forms a full\n32-bit PC-plus-sign-extended-immediate sum before reducing its upper\ntwelve bits to decide whether a taken prediction is safe. That late\ndecision feeds both fetch selection and the newly registered recovery\ntokens. Prior branch replay found only about 54,467 conditional misses\nand 13,735 JALRs; accuracy alone offers insufficient headroom. Fetch\nqueues repeatedly lost their saved cycles to timing, and pipelining\nBHT training regressed. Shorten prediction eligibility itself while\nretaining the champion's successful recovery and prediction policy.\n\nImplement a split direct-target generator in IF: calculate the low\ntwenty target bits in parallel with a fast carry-out certificate, and\nderive the in-range predicate from that carry, immediate sign and\ncomparisons of the registered PC's high twelve bits. A predicted\ntarget is always in the first 1 MiB, so its high bits can be zero\nwithout waiting for a sign-extension carry chain. This is one\npredictor timing change; retain the 128-entry bimodal table, exact\ntraining, direct JAL policy, sequential JALR policy and pipeline depth.\n\nLet P=PC[19:0], I=direct_imm[19:0], H=PC[31:20], S=direct_imm[31],\nand C be the unsigned carry-out of P+I. B and J immediates both have\ndirect_imm[31:20] equal to twelve copies of S. The exact modulo-32-bit\ntarget is inside the first 1 MiB iff\n((H==0) AND (C==S)) OR\n((H==0xfff) AND !S AND C) OR\n((H==1) AND S AND !C).\nPreserve all three terms, including wraparound from high addresses;\ndo not assume architectural PCs are already in the low memory region.\nUse two-bit modulo addition for alignment. When instruction kind,\nexisting BHT direction, alignment and this range certificate permit\nprediction, select {12'b0, low_target[19:0]}; otherwise select full\n32-bit PC+4. \n…[17639 of 20711 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:46d4761cf5afda80]…\nheck all architectural assertions, contiguous retirement order, exactly-once memory effects and training, and no wrong-path stores/divide starts. Retain unchanged formal including its ten-cycle liveness bound, real and ALTOPS pipeline/cosim gates, and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/markers. Measure actual marked cycles and all three Gowin options; acceptance requires median Fmax_Hz times 10/cycles strictly above 204.5453 iterations/s. Inspect timing to establish that live imem target arithmetic is absent from ordinary next-fetch selection.\nMakefile:112:cosim: cosim-build bench/programs/selftest.elf bench/programs/coremark.elf\nMakefile:137:fpga: cosim-build bench/programs/coremark.elf\nMakefile:140:timing:\ntools/eval/gowin.py:208:    ap.add_argument(\"--all-options\", action=\"store_true\",\ntest/cosim/build.sh:20:# NRET picks which RVFI port set main.cpp expects on `core`.\ntest/cosim/build.sh:24:NRET=\"${NRET:-2}\"\ntest/cosim/build.sh:55:  -CFLAGS \"-DNRET=$NRET\" \\\ncodex-bwrap-synthetic-mount-targets-1001\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
